window.CONTENT_BOOKS={"version":1,"title":"商英系","books":[{"key":"shangying-1","name":"商英教程1","units":[{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["identity (n. identity/identification; v. identify; adj. identifiable)","access (n. access/accessibility; v. access; adj. accessible; adv. accessibly)","conceive (n. conception; v. conceive; adj. conceivable; adv. conceivably)","discriminate (n. discrimination; v. discriminate; adj. discriminatory)","coordinate (n. coordination; v. coordinate; adj. coordinated)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It was an idea ___ and presented to the board of directors.","answer":"conceived","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Most fundamentally, a treatment is any specific educator behaviour that has an ___ effect on student behaviour.","answer":"identifiable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"There is substantial uncontroverted evidence that the RFP team worked in ___ with the bid team that proposed the proposals on behalf of Southern Power.","answer":"coordination","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"As with Facebook, developers have to ___ user data and may get to keep the revenue.","answer":"access","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Some of these laws will prohibit ___ against employees on the basis of their gender expression or genetic information.","answer":"discrimination","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"Adult passengers 18 and over must show valid ___ at the airport checkpoint in order to travel.","answer":"identification","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"To make information ___ you need to think about the language you use, and how you present it.","answer":"accessible","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Sarah suffered an ___ tragedy; she lost her best friend Jamie in a horrible accident.","answer":"inconceivable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The study shows the development of children's ability to ___ genuine from fake smiles.","answer":"discriminate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"China can only develop a successful domestic tourism industry if there is a well-___ effort between the government and the private travel industry.","answer":"coordinated","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 1 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Mr. Grasse thinks so highly of his business savvy that he says he intends to run ___ mayor next year.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Most companies are just hunkering down, crossing their fingers ___ the end of the Middle East crisis.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Coors Brewing says its content on Facebook and MySpace will adhere ___ the advertising and marketing code of the Beer Institute.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"She claimed that other students had engaged in similar expression, but that she had been singled ___ for punishment because of her ethnic background.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"Engineers, entrepreneurs, vendors and investors shared ideas and showed ___ technologies for reducing electricity, water and oil use.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Getting access to capital has become even harder since Sept. 11 as investors clamp ___ on new money.","answer":"down","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"That figure already is down significantly from about 46% ___ the aftermath of World War II, when European and Japanese factories lay in ruins.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Corporate travelers are well-versed in striking a balance between complying ___ their company policy and enjoying time on the road.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"I think there's a generation of leaders that went ___ a crisis and are going to manage and lead this way for the next 10 years.","answer":"through","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"There's no doubt that the global financial meltdown, at a cost of $20 trillion plus millions thrown ___ of work, had much to do with a \"progressive deregulation.\"","answer":"out","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["embarked","look the part","chill out","permeated","when it comes to","comes to mind","comprises","encompasses","overall","rendered","push the envelope","run the gamut","motif","wrestling","requisite"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Had the government not ___ on this policy, the great financial crisis of 2008 would not have occurred.","answer":"embarked","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"He doesn't act his age or ___ , but his birth certificate is telling it straight.","answer":"look the part","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"I want Scott to feel fulfilled, but how can I ask him to ___ on the hobbies without being a nag.","answer":"chill out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"It is perhaps the most striking evidence of the extent to which information technology has ___ the financial industry.","answer":"permeated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"It requires a different way of thinking for most companies ___ how much time and money should go into their giving initiatives.","answer":"when it comes to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Many emerging small businesses seem to try anything that ___ as long as it might make some money.","answer":"comes to mind","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Overall, the luxury market ___ 13% of all new-car sales in the USA.","answer":"comprises","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"PIM software is based on a concept called complex adaptive systems (CAS), a generic term that ___ new approaches to coping with complexity.","answer":"encompasses","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"That figure includes losses to the airlines, wasted time for passengers and the ___ cost to the economy.","answer":"overall","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"That was an allusion to Warrener's ears, ___ in red in the sketch, apparently from risqué remarks by the dancers.","answer":"rendered","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"The Apollo landing really did not ___ of physics, but was a tremendous engineering challenge.","answer":"push the envelope","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"The programs ___ from on-site management consulting to demonstrations of new technology.","answer":"run the gamut","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"The same \"A\" design was used as a logo ___ at their 2005 wedding.","answer":"motif","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"They were ___ with how to divide their $1.5 million estate among their three children.","answer":"wrestling","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Traditional companies need look only for the ___ technical expertise and work habits, while teams need skills like the ability to handle confrontations.","answer":"requisite","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 1 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"朋友、家人和邻居常常感到困惑，在这紧急的事件发生时不知道找谁来帮忙。(baffle, in the event of)","answer":"Friends, family and neighbors are often baffled about who to call for help in the event of such an emergency.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"共和党和民主党在反恐问题上目标一致但实现路径相异，因而更可能既相互对抗又互相妥协，成为了对立统一体。(odds, the same coin)","answer":"The Republican and Democratic parties have the same objectives in anti-terrorist issues, but reached by different pathways. Great odds are that they have become two sides of the same coin, opposing and compromising with each other.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"在某种程度上，职业评级的基础是教育程度，因而残疾少年经历的教育困难与其职业志向之间的联系或许在理解该项研究结果中发挥着重要作用。(likely, in part)","answer":"The ratings of occupations are based, in part, on levels of education. Therefore, it is likely the connection between educational difficulties experienced by adolescents with disabilities and occupational aspirations play an important role in understanding the research results.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"亚洲金融危机导致石油需求急速下降，油价一度下滑至一桶不到10美元，进而引发产量削减并取消了多个开采工程，这都不是什么秘密。(secret, plunge)","answer":"It is no secret that financial crises in Asia undercut demand for oil so rapidly that prices plunged for a time below $10 a barrel, prompting production cuts and the cancellation of several exploration projects.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"继早些时候媒体上出现的负面报道和社交媒体的激烈反应之后，ZARA所属的Inditex集团——全球第九大零售品牌和最大的服装公司，发表了致歉信。(backlash, apparel)","answer":"Following some early negative media coverage and social media backlash, Zara's parent company Inditex — the ninth largest retailer in the world, and the biggest apparel company, issued an apology.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 1 英译汉（穿出成功）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"In the book Dress for Success, John Molloy does not hand down dicta on \"good\" or \"bad\" taste in clothing. His purpose is to reveal what clothing is effective, i.e., what attire makes people view you as successful, powerful, or attractive. The clothes that best help men climb the corporate ladder are conservative suits, shirts, and ties. He interviewed over 15,000 executives to find out that, \"In matters of clothing, conservative, class-conscious conformity is absolutely essential to the individual success of the American business and professional man.\"","answer":"约翰·莫利在著作《穿出成功》中没有断言何为穿着品位的优劣。他旨在表明何为有效的穿着，即穿什么使你在他人眼里是成功者或权高者，或能引人目光。最能帮助男性在公司职阶上步步高升的衣服是保守的西装、衬衫和领带。他采访了15,000位公司管理者，发现\"穿着上遵从保守做派和阶层意识对美国商务领域和职场中的个人成功非常必要\"。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 1 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["as","case","enhance","if","increase","like","spending","that","true","upside","unless","way","what","whether","which"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"When looking to purchase a new car, we don't consider a car's safety or maintenance record ___ the car first looks good to us.","answer":"unless","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"When buying clothes, we don't care to learn how great the quality of the garment is ___ it doesn't look attractive to us.","answer":"if","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The same is ___ when we are in need of a professional.","answer":"true","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"We will not consider putting our trust in a professional, who doesn't look the ___ we think he/she should look.","answer":"way","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Unfortunately, this makes appearance \"everything\" in ___ a person will not be interested in learning more about something that does not \"appear\" to be what they want or like.","answer":"that","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"If you want people to trust and respect you as a professional, you first have to look ___ a trustworthy, respectable professional.","answer":"like","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"However, dressing like a professional doesn't mean ___ all your income on designer clothes or the latest fashion trends.","answer":"spending","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"A wardrobe engineer, named John Molloy, turned the business world ___ down with a modest book called Dress for Success.","answer":"upside","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"In it, he explains how a man can determine his own success or failure based on ___ he wears.","answer":"what","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"By reviewing the basics as they relate to dressing for chiropractic success, you can ___ your professional image and your credibility with patients.","answer":"enhance","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["reference (n. reference; v. refer/reference; adj. referenced/referential)","extension (n. extension; v. extend; adj. extensive/extended; adv. extensively)","excess (n. excess; v. exceed; adj. excessive; adv. excessively)","precedence (n. precedence/precede; v. precede; adj. (un)precedented/precedent)","symbol (n. symbol; v. symbolize; adj. symbolic; adv. symbolically)","benefit (n. benefit/beneficiary; v. benefit; adj. beneficial; adv. beneficially)","comparison (n. comparison; v. compare; adj. comparative/comparable; adv. comparatively)","contradiction (n. contradiction; v. contradict; adj. contradictory; adv. contradictorily)","popularity (n. (un)popularity; v. popularize; adj. (un)popular; adv. popularly)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"DHL allows you to track your express shipments using a personalized ___ number.","answer":"reference","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Kobe Bryant signed a two-year ___ with the Los Angeles Lakers in 2013. The five-time NBA champion announced his intention to retire when the deal expires following the 2015-16 campaign.","answer":"extension","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"During the first quarter of 2015, gross job gains ___ gross job losses in most industry sectors in 31 states.","answer":"exceeded","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"Economists are still arguing whether American economy is heading for recession, but everyone agrees that there has been a sharp slowdown after a decade of ___ expansion.","answer":"unprecedented","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Christians believed that God took a rib from Adam to make Eve, yet in modern times, many people have chosen to take the story ___.","answer":"symbolically","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"Outsourcing has become a viable and ___ business strategy that enables firms to restructure their distribution networks, spread risk and focus on future growth.","answer":"beneficial","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Official figures show that inflation edged up to 0.1% last month after ___ moderate falls in petrol and alcohol prices.","answer":"comparatively","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"It is precisely the proudest and most obstinate men who are the most liable to shift their position and ___ themselves in this sudden manner.","answer":"contradict","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The Chinese Cultural Festival in Moscow was held by the Confucius Institute of Moscow State University, aiming to ___ Chinese cultures including calligraphy, martial arts, folk dancing, traditional instruments and Peking opera.","answer":"popularize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Boys are encouraged to tough out difficult courses in ___ subjects, while girls, no matter how smart, receive fewer arguments from their parents or teachers if they drop a physics class.","answer":"unpopular","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 2 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Jane is an excellent communicator with a warm and professional demeanor and a great sense of humor. She enjoys nurturing long-term relationships with her clients, whom she holds ___ high regard as friends.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"During WWII, some black soldiers who experienced cruel and humiliating treatment fell into depression and eventually killed themselves. Some referred ___ their death as murder, while many choose to forget.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"We tend to assign esteem, identity and status ___ physical things and fashion is an easy way to do this.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"I see the Russian soldiers standing ___ the threshold of their native land, guarding the fields which their fathers have tilled from time immemorial.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"Those brands that many people trust to provide clean, natural products are shelling ___ millions to ensure that the public doesn't know GMOs are used in their daily foods.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Taking advantage of the hydropower, Ethiopia hopes to reap benefits ___ its eco-friendly rail projects to ease urban traffic congestion and reduce carbon emissions and pollution.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Linguists find that all languages change ___ time — albeit at different rates, in three main aspects: vocabulary, sentence structure and pronunciations.","answer":"over","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"This hypnosis found a subject, grabbed his attention and let him experience the feeling of having his hand stuck ___ his head, feet stuck ___ the floor.","answer":"to, to","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"There's an old saying that ___ polite company, it's not proper to talk about religion or politics, so stick to neutral subjects like the weather to avoid conversational confrontation.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Apart from the source of energy, a nuclear energy plant is ___ essence no different from any fossil fuel power plant. Both use the energy source to generate heat to drive turbines that generate electricity.","answer":"in","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["traced back to","endowed with","preceded by","continuum","complement","entail","Virtue","counterparts","niche","turned out to be","make sense","renowned for","impulse","dubious","typical"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"According to a team of researchers from Copenhagen University, all blue-eyed people can be ___ one ancestor who lived 10,000 years ago near the Black Sea.","answer":"traced back to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Many travellers described it as a prosperous city rich ___ natural resources.","answer":"endowed with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The presentation was ___ an introduction of the basic concepts and a short video show of the panel discussion.","answer":"preceded by","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Most members of a collectivistic culture will hold values at the collectivistic end of the continuum, although each will be at a different spot on the ___ , and some will even be at the individualistic end.","answer":"continuum","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The project could mobilise additional resources from development partners that could ___ the limited resources allocated by government.","answer":"complement","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Falling prices would ___ a vicious circle of lower production, more bankruptcies and even more unemployment.","answer":"entail","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"___ may be defined as a habit of mind in harmony with reason and the order of nature. It has four parts: wisdom, justice, courage, temperance.","answer":"Virtue","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Under pressure from industry groups, top U.S. officials have travelled to China and worked with their ___ to re-establish a full cyber dialogue.","answer":"counterparts","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"Many companies ended up branching out and expanding their business. Only those that remain focused on its ___ area of specialization have key advantages over larger or more diversified businesses.","answer":"niche","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"To our great surprise the real murderer in this detective story ___ the narrator's best friend.","answer":"turned out to be","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"With his help in putting all the scattered information together, the research finally starts to ___ now.","answer":"make sense","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"Wieden+Kennedy, the advertising company ___ its creative and bold work, helps Nike become a winner in terms of global positioning in the 2014 World Cup.","answer":"renowned for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Different from the physical retailing stores, virtual environment, graphics, pop-up windows, audio, colours, streaming video and so on are all stimuli that lead to ___ buying.","answer":"impulse","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"They indulged in some highly ___ business practices to obtain their current position in the market.","answer":"dubious","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"A combination of salty, sweet, creamy, spicy, hot and pungent flavors is ___ of Indian meal. The basic menu usually comprises starch, a meat or fish main dish, vegetables, and chutney.","answer":"typical","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 2 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"当今社会有着过多的号称权威而实际上却自相矛盾的理论，我们需要独立思考，然后再作出判断。(an excess of, turn out to be, contradictory)","answer":"There are an excess of theories in today's society that claim to be authoritative but turn out to be contradictory. We need to think independently and then make our own judgment.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"由于在作品中深入刻画了文化多样性对人心灵产生的冲击，他被提名今年的诺贝尔文学奖。他同时也在世界非物质文化遗产(intangible cultural heritage)保护工作中扮演了重要角色。(diversity, play a ... role in)","answer":"Because his works vividly depict the impact of cultural diversity on the human mind, he has been nominated for this year's Nobel Prize in Literature. He also plays an important role in the protection of the world's intangible cultural heritage.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"由于忙碌的生活方式削弱了亲情，各个家庭不再像以往一样比邻而居，要保持联系只能通过有意识地保持重要的仪式和传统。(ritual, proximity)","answer":"As busy lifestyles have weakened family bonds, families no longer live in close proximity to one another as they used to; to stay connected, they can only consciously maintain important rituals and traditions.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"关于自然界平衡的观念长期以来主宰了生态研究和管理，所以生态环境保护者从未对此心存疑虑，认为人类介入生态环境破坏了平衡。(equilibrium, dubious)","answer":"The notion of a balance of nature has long dominated ecological research and management, so environmentalists have never been dubious about it, believing that human intervention in the ecological environment has destroyed the equilibrium.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"蜂蜜中含有浓缩的维生素、矿物质和营养成分，为你的身体提供营养和活力。(nourish, a dose of sth)","answer":"Honey contains concentrated vitamins, minerals and nutrients, which provide your body with a dose of nourishment and vitality.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 2 英译汉（四大风味与八大菜系）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The diversity of geography, climate, customs and products have led to the evolution of what are called the \"Four Flavours\" and \"Eight Cuisines,\" but as catering is a living art, sub-classifications continue to increase. Cuisine in China is a harmonious integration of colour, redolence, taste, shape and the fineness of the instruments. For the cooking process, chefs pick choice and various ingredients and seasonings while employing unparalleled complicated skills handed down from their fathers, ever aspiring to their ideal of perfection for all the senses. Among the many cooking methods they use are boiling, stewing, braising, frying, steaming, crisping, baking, and simmering and so on. When they finish their masterpieces they are arranged on a variety of plates and dishes so that they are a real pleasure to view, to smell and ultimately to savour. The facility to partake of these delights is also distinctive — chopsticks!","answer":"多样化的地理、气候、风俗和物产促成了大家所说的\"四大风味\"和\"八大菜系\"的发展演变，而由于餐饮是一门活生生的艺术，其种类还在继续增多。中国菜肴是色、香、味、形的统一，也融合了器具的精致。在烹饪过程中，厨师采用从父辈传下来的无与伦比的复杂手艺，精选上等食材和多种配料及调味品，一直渴望实现多重感官的完美感受。在众多烹饪方法中，他们使用煮、炖、焖、煎、蒸、炸、烤、煨等方法，大功告成之后，他们再将美食置于各种不同的盘碟之上，以使观赏效果、嗅觉效果和品尝效果达到最佳。享受这些美食的工具也十分独特，是筷子！","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 2 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["a","aspects","basis","circumstances","diets","do","food","on","quotation","regarding","saying","that","way","which"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Philosophy of food finds its ___ on the idea that food is a mirror.","answer":"basis","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"You may have heard about the ___ \"We are what we eat.\"","answer":"saying","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Well, there is more to say ___ this relation.","answer":"regarding","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Eating mirrors the making of a self, ___ is,","answer":"that","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"the array of decisions and ___ that bring us to eat the way we","answer":"circumstances","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"the way we ___.","answer":"do","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"In them, we can see reflected ___ detailed and comprehensive image of ourselves.","answer":"a","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Philosophy of food reflects ___ the ethical, political, social, artistic, identity-defining","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"the ethical, political, social, artistic, identity-defining ___ of food.","answer":"aspects","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"It spurs from the challenge to more actively ponder our ___ and eating habits so as to understand who we are in a deeper, more authentic way.","answer":"diets","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["ambivalence (n. ambivalence; adj. ambivalent)","paralysis (n. paralysis; v. paralyze; adj. paralyzing)","patronize (v. patronize; adj. patronizing)","escalate (n. escalation; v. escalate; adj. escalating)","versatility (n. versatility; adj. versatile)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Many of Wall Street's top firms are similarly ___ , with analysts under the same roof offering conflicting analysis and advice.","answer":"ambivalent","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Even extreme events — winning the lottery or suffering a ___ accident — affect long-term happiness to a lesser degree than most people suppose.","answer":"paralyzing","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"The low switching rate reflects the fact that consumers of small banks ___ them for other reasons — among other things, because of the more personal attention.","answer":"patronize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"There has been tension and ___ over Fred Kirby's insistence that he should govern the family's business affairs.","answer":"ambivalence","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"It would average about 3.1 percent because of ___ costs for programs like Social Security and Medicare as baby boomers age and receive benefits.","answer":"escalating","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"I live not far from a kind but occasionally ___ lady who fancies herself an expert gardener.","answer":"patronizing","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"The advantages of offering such experiences not only enhance learners' efficiency but also ___ their interests.","answer":"escalate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Doing repertory demands ___ and pushes actors out of a comfort zone.","answer":"versatility","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"It can cause corporate ___ when executives and middle managers become afraid to make decisions.","answer":"paralysis","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Compared with other mapping sites, Google Maps is simpler, more ___ , and easier to use on mobile devices.","answer":"versatile","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 3 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"When organic food became popular, certain stores were quick to jump ___ the bandwagon and promote it.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"When the factory closed down, the workers all found themselves ___ the same boat.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Building a school before knowing the age of the population is putting the cart ___ the horse.","answer":"before","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"We seek to blend environmental and economic needs ___ a fashion that allows for: clean water, clean air, fish and wildlife and diverse lifestyles.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"More than 2.3 million comments have been received by the Forest Service with ___ of 95 percent of them in favour of the strongest protections possible.","answer":"upwards","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"The ability to view evidence from both perspectives strikes us as essential ___ the advancement of an evidence-based practice culture.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"The e-Nanoflex system uses a small amount of the phone's computing capacity to filter this noise before transmitting information ___ to cloud computers for further processing.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Don't let the noise of others' opinions drown ___ your own inner voice.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"Software designers and engineers have begun to incorporate functions ___ those applications specifically to limit the possibility of failure.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Wrigley's speculative interest soon deepened to enchantment ___ the island's pristine beauty.","answer":"with","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["glimpse","economical","breakdowns","In addition to","Small wonder","compete for","soared","overshadowed","Based on","enables","drowned out","banned","transition","end up","epitomizes"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"If you want a ___ of the post-recession American workplace, stop in at any Anderen Bank branch in Orlando.","answer":"glimpse","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Traveling by Greyhound is ___ . Thus lots of people go around the country by it.","answer":"economical","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The computer has three ___ this morning! It must have been infected by a deadly virus.","answer":"breakdowns","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"___ the benefits I have mentioned, doing exercises regularly may help to improve one's self-image.","answer":"In addition to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Badminton player Zhang Ning won the second Olympic gold medal at the age of 33. ___ she was in tears when interviewed by a CCTV journalist after the match.","answer":"Small wonder","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Athletes from 28 countries ___ the event, and only the best can make it to the final.","answer":"compete for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Prices ___ as inflation got worse.","answer":"soared","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"The beauty of Beijing Siheyuan (quadrangle) is far from being ___ by skyscrapers and high rises. Together, they present an image of an old Beijing with the new.","answer":"overshadowed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"___ the evidences in hand, the judge ruled him guilty.","answer":"Based on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Yoga exercise ___ me to adjust my breathing and concentrate well.","answer":"enables","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"The audience's cheering ___ the actor's words. Seeing this, he waved his hand to them.","answer":"drowned out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"Since the government ___ free plastic bags in supermarkets and stores, many small plastic bag plants have closed up.","answer":"banned","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Hobby usually plays an important part in a smooth ___ from full-time work to full-time retirement.","answer":"transition","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"\"Loaf around all day, you will ___ accomplishing nothing.\" Father used to warn us.","answer":"end up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The book, with its punch lines, ___ the end-of-millennium spirit.","answer":"epitomizes","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 3 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"公司的目标之一是建立一个针对某些特定人员的实时档案，从而确定谁来参与某个项目，以及事件如何展开等。(unfold)","answer":"One of the firm's aims seems to be to create real-time dossiers on particular individuals that will establish who is involved in the project, and how events might unfold.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"国家计委努力把这一精辟论断贯彻到机构改革中，凡是市场能解决的，坚决交由市场解决。(insight)","answer":"The State Planning Council has worked to apply this key insight to the structural reform. Anything that can be solved by the market will certainly be given to the market to solve.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"我国每年约有1300万的农村人口涌向城市，这个数字相当于现在整个北京市的人口。(flood)","answer":"Every year, about 13 million rural people flood into China's cities, equivalent to the current population of Beijing.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"壮观的午夜焰火表演将为庆祝活动增添色彩，乐手们则会挨家挨户地唱着祝福新年好运的歌。(add to)","answer":"A spectacular midnight fireworks display will add to the celebration and musicians will walk from house to house singing good-luck greetings for the New Year.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"穆尔森(Moissan)发明了一种具有独创性的制作方法，这种方法不像我的方法那么危险和昂贵。(entail)","answer":"Moissan has devised a process of great ingenuity which does not entail the danger and expense of mine.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 3 英译汉（自行车与汽车）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The middle class increasingly forgoes bicycles — the environmentally friendly and energy-efficient transport — in favour of the car. Some four million bikes now compete for road space with more than two million cars, and a quick glance at the newly constructed overpasses and ring roads clearly shows which means of transport has been getting priority. Fewer and fewer people are riding bikes because of the inconvenience and the increased dangers that cars bring to the road. However, the improvement in the state economy, the traffic situation and city management does not mean that we should say a final and complete farewell to the bicycle. Some people will still choose this non-polluting, small and green transport tool.","answer":"越来越多的中产阶级放弃了自行车这种绿色环保、节省能源的交通工具而选择购买汽车，现有约四百万辆的自行车与两百多万辆的汽车抢占道路，看看建设中的立交桥和环形公路，不言而喻哪种出行方式已被优先考虑。由于骑车不便以及汽车给骑车者带来的危险在增加，骑自行车的人越来越少。然而，发展国家经济、改善交通状况和城市管理并不意味着我们要与自行车永久地作别——仍然有人会选择这种无污染、小巧和绿色的交通工具。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 3 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["annually","buyers","competition","especially","importantly","living","economic","well","regarded","market"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"China's two-decade-long ___ growth is fueling the ongoing car craze.","answer":"economic","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The national economy has doubled since 1990, boosting people's ___ standard,","answer":"living","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"___ in major cities and along the coast.","answer":"especially","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Annual household incomes in major cities are reaching or exceeding the 4,000-dollar mark ___ as a take-off point for private auto ownership on a massive scale.","answer":"regarded","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"At the same time, banks as ___ as major carmakers in China are plunging into auto-credit business.","answer":"well","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"More ___ , as Western and Asian auto giants hasten to squeeze into the world's fastest-growing auto","answer":"importantly","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"hasten to squeeze into the world's fastest-growing auto ___ ,","answer":"market","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"car prices have dropped significantly in the last four years thanks to ___ among these giants.","answer":"competition","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"China's auto production has been growing by 15 percent ___ on average in the last decade and this year China will produce at least 5 million motor vehicles, about half of them cars.","answer":"annually","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"As a host of new models debut each year to lure would-be ___ , a series of price wars have been reshaping the industry since 2000.","answer":"buyers","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["grace (n. grace; v. grace; adv. gracefully)","civilization (n. civilization; v. civilize; adj. civilized)","hospitality (n. hospitality; adj. hospitable; adv. hospitably)","controversy (n. controversy; v. controvert; adj. controversial; adv. controversially)","sustainability (n. sustainability; adj. sustainable; adv. sustainably)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"What a wonderful win-win story to ___ the front page of The Post on Saturday.","answer":"grace","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Whenever a race goes national, Obama seems to feel ___ compelled to comment.","answer":"controversy","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Fresh signs of radiation leaks have raised questions about the ___ of the government's feed-and-bleed approach.","answer":"sustainability","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"\"The folk school was started by outsiders as a way to ___ mountain people,\" says Jan Davidson, the school's executive director.","answer":"civilize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"It's a ___ idea that has attracted criticism from other climate scientists and has been assailed by climate deniers.","answer":"controversial","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"I found the beaches still beautiful, the breeze refreshingly seductive, the islanders friendly and ___.","answer":"hospitable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Echoing the floral motif wallpaper behind it, the lamp resembles a stylized iris with a ___ arcing stem and a Vaseline glass shade.","answer":"gracefully","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"The so-called community, with all its might, pounces on a small ___ country, and ruins infrastructure that has been built over generations.","answer":"civilized","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"You need a path back to a budget, and that does require some ___ belt-tightening.","answer":"sustainable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"I realize the deep truth of Ojiichan's words, that the tradition of ___ , kindness, and openness on the island must trace its roots to the pilgrim's own openhearted quest.","answer":"hospitality","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 4 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Burners partake ___ the cultural equivalent of a potluck supper: everyone is expected to create the meal.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Lighthearted graphics and simple rhymes give your little one and you the chance to giggle ___ loud at the thought of animals taking the driver's seat.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"The two are good friends and talk often, but she admits their conversations can stray ___ awkward territory.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"The last of the guests had retreated in the early hours of the morning, leaving the king in the company ___ his most reliant confidants.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The view from atop 10,450-foot Liberty Pass may cause you to rub your eyes ___ disbelief at the sheer beauty of northeastern Nevada's pristine Ruby Mountains.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Her parents and brother left for America, while his relatives relocated ___ France.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"She went to the far end of that long room lined ___ portraits of the obscure daughters and younger sons of various British kings.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Firefighters say winds have started to die ___ , making their work a little easier.","answer":"down","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"John has never been able to find a job and has lived ___ his parents all his life.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Ford, like other automakers, has been cautious ___ increasing production capacity after closing plants and eliminating tens of thousands of jobs in the last decade.","answer":"about","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["fetching","grazing","meager","yawning","contribute to","mighty","status quo","concession","trudge","crouch","harness","weather-beaten","bathed in","sumptuous","abundance"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"A solid male audience seems possible, considering \"Twilight\" features a sturdy male with superpowers, a pack of ravenous bloodsuckers and ___ young women, both human and vampire.","answer":"fetching","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The center sits outside of town, within view of ___ cows.","answer":"grazing","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"But there are other explanations for ___ job growth than income inequality — many of them entwined.","answer":"meager","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"In the small attached grocery store Barbara bought instant coffee and breakfast staples, and the cashier asked without much interest ___ if she was enjoying her visit.","answer":"yawning","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"I love working with students as they ___ these efforts and create their own web-based knowledge-building centers.","answer":"contribute to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Wading a small stream for smallmouth bass is a fun way to spend a ___ summer day, but scoring big fish in this kind of water can be far more challenging than hooking up on a river or deep lake.","answer":"mighty","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"\"The ___ in American public education for decades and decades has put all the risk on the students,\" says Bill Sanders, a retired University of Tennessee professor and senior research fellow at the SAS Institute.","answer":"status quo","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Google, too, has made a big ___ to Apple's approach, signaling with its acquisition of Motorola Mobility last year that it will also design its own devices.","answer":"concession","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"Footprint upon footprint, they ___ through wild olive, purple sage and mesquite, past the cattle, over the scattered white sand dunes that fool the eye and gulp the foot up to the ankle.","answer":"trudge","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Somehow she's got to be able to jump in the back of that truck and ___ down without being detected.","answer":"crouch","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"We really need to ___ the power of capitalism at a very big scale.","answer":"harness","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"\"We don't have drinking water and there's not enough food to feed the children,\" says the farmer, who has a ___ face and torn clothes.","answer":"weather-beaten","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Everyone had been told to wear gold, and the stage area inside the Apex was ___ a soft, jewel-toned glow.","answer":"bathed in","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"As elegantly ___ as they are imaginatively extravagant, Kuniyoshi's greatest prints represent turbulent, epic visions of human protagonists battling supernatural beings.","answer":"sumptuous","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Australia is blessed with an ___ of natural resources and has become China's leading supplier of coal and iron ore.","answer":"abundance","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 4 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"由于解除管制(deregulation)及其带给旅客的危险，我决定两年内不去那个国家旅行了。(bring about)","answer":"As a result of deregulation and the danger to travelers it has brought about, I make up my mind that I will not make that country my travel destination in recent two years.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"我们在佩特拉(Petra)加入了旅行团大巴的人群参观这座纳巴泰人(Nabateans)的古代都城，发现这玫瑰色的沙漠城市美丽壮观得无法用言语来形容。(do justice to)","answer":"We joined the tour-bus crowds in Petra to visit the ancient capital of the Nabateans and found that no words could do justice to the beauty and grandeur of the rose-red city of the desert.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"从人们对即将推出的预告片的反应来看，这部电影一定能成为这位年轻有为的导演又一成功之作。(judge by, be bound to)","answer":"Judging by the response to the upcoming trailers, this movie is bound to be another success of this young and promising director.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"这个满脸风霜的老人告诉我们：\"我们很节俭。我们可以靠利息生活，省下本金，让孩子们出去闯荡挣钱。\"(weather-beaten, live off)","answer":"The old man with a weather-beaten face told us: \"We're thrifty. We can live off our interest, save the principal and let the kids go off and have a hoot.\"","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"她写过一些引起争议的诗，令她声名鹊起，但是时间一长，公众的关注很快平息下来。(controversial, die down)","answer":"She wrote some controversial poems, which brought her instant fame, but the publicity soon died down over time.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 4 英译汉（度假逃逸）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Whatever form vacation takes, we keep on doing it — we may even want to do it more to escape all the talk of terror and war. We are escapaholics convinced that this time we will definitely \"get away from it all\", returning to the office slimmer, tanned and desperately keen to read a spread sheet. The Great European Vacation lives on because, as with everything else, anticipation often beats act, and all that preparation with brochures, bookings, tickets, servicing the car and packing suitcases, and, above all, counting down the days. But escaping can be stressful. A survey published this week by the British recruitment firm Reed found that 22% of 5,000 British workers said they suffer a syndrome Reed calls \"Pre-Holiday Stress\", that sense of panic caused by trying to get everything in order before leaving.","answer":"不管度假采取何种形式，我们还是乐此不疲，我们甚至想更频繁地度假以逃避关于恐怖和战争的话题。我们有逃离癖，深信这次我们一定可以永久地逃离所有的一切，回到办公室时会变得苗条、黝黑，热切地想阅读那些电子表格。欧洲度假热潮经久不衰，因为和其他事物一样，预期往往高于行动。前戏让人兴奋，比如看介绍手册、预订、买票、检修汽车、准备行李等，最让人兴奋的是倒计时。但是逃离也可能充满压力，根据英国招聘机构里德公司这周发布的调查表明：受调查的5000名英国雇员中的22%表示他们在假前感到受到一系列综合症状的折磨，源自于想在离开前将一切打理妥当而感到的一种恐慌，里德公司将此称之为\"假前压力综合症\"。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 4 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["annoyingly","before","by","gain","in","of","off","on","packed","stomach","that","throat","unclaimed","up","when"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"In the islands where surfing began, the waves on that particular day were a disappointment — mushy, chest high, and ___ infrequent.","answer":"annoyingly","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Still, Hawaiians have never needed much ___ an excuse to grab a board and hit the ocean,","answer":"of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"and the takeoff zone was ___ : teens on shortboards, moms on longboards, grade-schoolers on bodyboards.","answer":"packed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Straddling my surfboard ___ the deep water beside the reef,","answer":"in","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"I surveyed the crowd with a knot in my ___ , feeling that I didn't belong.","answer":"stomach","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"For half an hour I floated near the takeoff zone, waiting for my chance, ___ I finally spotted what appeared to be an","answer":"before","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"what appeared to be an ___ wave.","answer":"unclaimed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"I spun my board toward the beach and paddled hard. But just as I ___ speed, a stone-faced teenager on a bodyboard finned up the same wave.","answer":"gain","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"He planted his hand firmly ___ my shoulder","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and pushed me ___ the wave, simultaneously propelling himself down its face. I gave up and paddled in.","answer":"off","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["desperate (n. desperateness; adj. desperate; adv. desperately)","approve (n. approval; v. approve; adj. approved)","assume (n. assumption; v. assume; adj. assumed; adv. assumedly)","deceive (n. deception; v. deceive; adj. deceptive)","initiate (n. initial/initiative; v. initiate; adj. initial)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Upon my word, I never saw a young woman so ___ in love in my life.","answer":"desperately","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Nigerians have been outraged by what they've seen as government ___ inaction. Contrary to government claims, none of the girls have been rescued.","answer":"initial","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Paula took it upon herself — unasked, entirely on her own ___ — to begin conducting interviews with strangers to see what they thought about the election season.","answer":"initiative","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"Departments may also admit students with a good Bachelor's degree with relevant research or working experience on a case-by-case basis, subject to ___ by the Board of Graduate Studies.","answer":"approval","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"There is plenty of research on body movement and ___ , which could be used in employment screening and security checkpoint at the airport.","answer":"deception","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"Once ___ , your refund request will be processed within 7 working days to the original form of payment and should show in your account within the next 5-7 working days.","answer":"approved","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"I was shocked to see that people still subscribe to the same old American Dream, following a prescribed lifestyle and ___ in predictable life stages that they do not want.","answer":"assumedly","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"The associations we have with certain names shape how we see ourselves and so may have an effect on our confidence and ___ role in society.","answer":"assumed","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The world is ___ for oil and the war in the Middle East and threat of a nuclear armed Iran intensified the fear of an oil supply interruption, which produced the market speculation to push oil prices even higher.","answer":"desperate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Bank of America charged customers for the service without authorization, enrolled them through ___ marketing, and improperly denied benefits, the class action lawsuit alleged.","answer":"deceptive","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 5 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Our product line has grown and varied, to keep up ___ the ever-changing expectations in the market.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"These proposals are in line ___ our present policy.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"The real issue is not whether you can buy a house, but whether your first home will be a good deal — a property that makes sense in terms ___ pricing, financing, condition, comfort and the potential for appreciation.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Industrialists must move fast to take advantage ___ new opportunities in Eastern Europe.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"If you wish to figure ___ the entire price of your purchase with the sales tax added in, multiply the price by the tax rate plus one.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Just increasing your monthly payment by a few dollars can dramatically cut down ___ the time it takes to pay your debt, along with the total interest paid.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Increase in government borrowing will result in higher interest rates, which will crowd ___ private investment and consumption.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Under this assumption, one third of the family's expenditures would be for food no matter how far it had cut back ___ its total expenditures.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"If all your goals have been achieved and nothing gets better, just live ___ it outside of work.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"The credit card business is down, and more borrowers are defaulting ___ loans.","answer":"on","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["straighten out","run up against","spiral","wind up (doing sth)","consequence","be saddled with","discretionary","conspicuous","covetous","fortuitous","dwarf","in ... terms","precautionary","to be worth (sth/doing sth)","equivalent","wind up","running up against","saddled with","worth","consequences","spiralled into","covetousness"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Bloom pushed the UAW (United Auto Workers) to take Chrysler stock but the union wanted cash, not stock that might ___ being worthless.","answer":"wind up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"It was an age of ___ consumption — those who had money like to display it.","answer":"conspicuous","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The government is ___ considerable opposition to its tax reforms.","answer":"running up against","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Warnings were given that the next collapse is ___ to that of 2008 — merely a dress rehearsal for what the world will face soon.","answer":"equivalent","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"While South Africa's nine largest municipalities have shown an improvement in the management of their finances, some municipalities such as Johannesburg are still ___ bad debt, mainly because of unfavourable economic conditions.","answer":"saddled with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Hunter S. Thompson, an American journalist once said, \"Anything ___ doing, is doing right.\"","answer":"worth","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"I would make an appointment with him to ___ a couple of things.","answer":"straighten out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Eligible individuals may reduce ___ savings if they know their medical expenses will be paid by the government.","answer":"precautionary","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"This is hardly a ___ achievement, the result of a campaign strategy that relied not on getting the vote out but on restraining it, at least for a key demographic.","answer":"fortuitous","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"The company said it plans ___ cuts in spending and will closely manage other operating expenses to further control costs.","answer":"discretionary","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"An economic crisis may have tremendous ___ for our global security.","answer":"consequences","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"During the campaign calling on students to write pro-Trump chalk messages on college and university campuses, schools nationwide ___ a chalk war and mass hysteria over pro-Trump messages.","answer":"spiralled into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"A learning disability is a neurological disorder. ___ simple ___ ; a learning disability results from a difference in the way a person's brain is \"wired\".","answer":"In ... terms","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Show him some money and stir up his ___ , and you may lead him as with a halter.","answer":"covetousness","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Physics is the present-day ___ of what used to be called natural philosophy, from which most of present-day sciences arose.","answer":"Equivalent","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 5 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"他上周顺利地通过了面试，得到了人生的第一份工作。(ace, land)","answer":"He aced the interview last week and landed the first job in his life.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"新措施旨在减少不请自来的电话推销。(cut back on, solicitation)","answer":"The new measures are aimed at cutting back on intrusive telephone solicitations.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"利用人们对健康的心理需求，该产品被吹嘘为纯天然的。(tout, take advantage of)","answer":"The product is touted as being completely natural, taking advantage of people's psychological need for health.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"这项针对解决学生贷款拖欠问题的提议被证明是难以实现的。(default, elusive)","answer":"The proposed solution to the problem of student loan default proves to be elusive.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"中国预防性储蓄的突然上升使得消费者市场更加不稳定。(volatile, spike)","answer":"The consumer market has become more volatile with the spike in precautionary savings in China.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 5 英译汉（储蓄与消费）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The two major players in the global economy, the U.S. and China, are operating at opposite ends of the saving spectrum. Thrifty Chinese have taken saving to excess, while profligate Americans have spent their way into debt. Neither of these trends is sustainable — they lead to destabilizing economic and political developments for both nations — and a better balance must be struck. China needs to convert excess saving into consumption, while the U.S. needs to end its buying binge and rediscover the art of saving.","answer":"全球经济的两大玩家，美国和中国，在储蓄问题上走向了两个极端。节俭的中国人积累了过量的储蓄金，而浪费的美国人却挥霍无度、负债累累。这两种趋势都不能再持续下去——这会导致两国经济的不稳定和政局的变化——必须寻求一个更好的平衡点。中国需要把过多的储蓄转变为消费，而美国则需结束无节制的花钱，重新找到积蓄的有效方法。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 5 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["issue","over","use","practice","balance","with","losing","conservative","make","attract"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Facing the large potential market, banks have been racing to ___ credit cards since the business shifted into high gear in China in 2003.","answer":"issue","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The competition has intensified with card issuers bombarding the market ___ cash bonuses and other gifts","answer":"with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"to win ___ consumers.","answer":"over","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Banks try to ___ more customers by offering various perks, cooperation with stores, airlines, hotels and even universities.","answer":"attract","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"However, most banks are ___ money in their credit card businesses as a large portion of the cards have apparently never been used since they were issued.","answer":"losing","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"A report issued by 51 Credit.com and Analysis International shows that only 20 to 40 percent of the credit cards issued are put into ___ with a large amount of cards \"sleeping.\"","answer":"use","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"For one reason, a traditional ___ spending culture is making the credit card business in China much harder.","answer":"conservative","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"\"Chinese feel more comfortable with the ___ of spending the money they really own,\" the McKinsey report points out.","answer":"practice","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"It says that 94 percent of credit card holders pay off the ___ of their cards","answer":"balance","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"before they have to ___ any interest payments.","answer":"make","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-wordFill-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["mobility (n. mobility; adj. mobile)","literacy (n. literacy; adj. literate; adv. literally)","immigrant (n. immigrant/immigration; v. immigrate)","access (n. access/accessibility; v. access; adj. accessed/accessible)","erode (n. erosion; v. erode; adj. eroding)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"They are more likely than public companies to make big bets and take big risks, and better than lone entrepreneurs at making things happen because they can ___ far more resources.","answer":"access","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Europe's current policy rewards refugees who are young, strong and ___ enough to reach its shores — precisely those in least need of help.","answer":"mobile","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Traditionally arable land may not have been quite as safe as houses, but it has always been a safe place to bury one's cash, metaphorically if not ___ , and this becomes even more important in a recession.","answer":"literally","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"For various reasons, ___ from China, Japan and Korea have thrived in America, outshining groups descended from other ancestors.","answer":"immigrants","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"The first surprise came in June, when the Pew Research Centre reported that Asians were ___ to the United States in higher numbers than Latinos.","answer":"immigrating","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"Even where shops are readily ___ , consumers often go \"showrooming,\" looking at goods in physical outlets but buying them more cheaply online.","answer":"accessible","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Car sharing, either through car clubs run by the big rental firms or peer-to-peer services, will be far easier when communication between vehicles and potential passengers is seamless and any car can be ___ and operated securely by any smartphone.","answer":"accessed","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"The products concerned are available only to M-PESA customers and can be ___ only via a mobile phone.","answer":"accessed","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The market sank lower, ___ the government's reserves as well as its credibility.","answer":"eroding","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"The best family companies work hard to prevent this ___ of trust over time by holding themselves to higher standards than the rest.","answer":"erosion","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-idioms-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 6 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Preliminary analyses indicated that GWI case status was strongly associated with veterans' reports of having been in Iraq, Kuwait, or both during deployment, ___ of the duration of time spent in those areas.","answer":"regardless","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"If the business is profitable, maybe, just maybe, the family can break ___ of poverty.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Amid fears that another recession was just ___ the corner, they gave up plan to open another new outlet.","answer":"around","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Retailers are trying more and more to tap ___ this logic — catering to customers by getting to know what they may be looking for based on where they live, and likely increasing sales in the process.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"A record 6.8 million Californians, nearly 1 in 5 of the state's residents, went ___ health insurance at some time during 2006, according to figures released Tuesday by the U.S. Census Bureau.","answer":"without","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Students asked questions about their midterm exam, but many grappled ___ a bigger question: What does a destabilized economy mean for their future?","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Eric Weiner digs deep to peel back the complex layers comprising modern Wall Street, letting the key figures speak ___ themselves.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"A frenzy of port, road and pipeline building in reforming Myanmar will connect ___ some long neglected bits of Asia.","answer":"upon","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"In a day when computers are a staple ___ nearly every aspect of business and investing, the NYSE sets itself apart from its competitors.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"The Federal Reserve can counteract inflation by pulling more money out ___ of the excess reserves, which will tighten the money supply by reducing banks' power to lend, thus fighting inflation.","answer":"up","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-complete-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["cutting-edge","document","immerse","pursue","respond","tap","differentiate","fuel","possess","prohibit","yield","indicate","moderation","pledge","track","responding","pursuit","documented","yielded","prohibitions","tracking","fuelled","indicating","immersion","pledged"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Thanks to a ___ IT industry, the country has developed tools for digital forensics and tracking cybercrime.","answer":"cutting-edge","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Transit providers are firms whose job is to link up Internet service providers which, in turn, offer Internet access to individuals, businesses, governments, or anyone else who wishes to ___ into the web.","answer":"tap","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Whatever the answer, the data imply that hotels wanting to manage their presence online need to pay more attention to the pleasant task of ___ to praise than to the punishing labour of calming angry clients.","answer":"responding","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"But the fallout will inevitably call into question Chief Executive Martin Winterkorn's control of the business, and his dogged ___ of becoming the world's largest car manufacturer.","answer":"pursuit","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The biography contains no new facts about Geoffrey Chaucer, author of \"The Canterbury Tales,\" whose barely ___ 14th-century life has long frustrated scholars.","answer":"documented","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"But his projects for economic development, including agricultural and economic overhauls, have ___ few positive results.","answer":"yielded","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Its economy is struggling and its polity is fragile; but Tunisia's pragmatism and ___ have nurtured hope in a wretched region and a troubled world.","answer":"moderation","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Labor productivity in Singapore has contracted in two of the past three years, a sign that its workers don't ___ the skills and initiative they require.","answer":"possess","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The Ming Chinese banned large ships; the Shogun Japanese, firearms; the medieval Italians, silk-spinning; Americans in the 1920s, alcohol. Such ___ can last a long time, but eventually they come to an end, so long as there is competition.","answer":"prohibitions","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"To try to keep up with all these changes, Mr. Fung has kitted out a shopping mall in Shanghai with technologies from IBM that allow detailed ___ of shoppers on site and online.","answer":"tracking","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"FedEx Corp. said on Monday that it expects holiday shipments to increase 12% between Black Friday and Christmas Eve, ___ by growth in e-commerce shopping.","answer":"fuelled","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"More data is released, ___ that the economy is slowing down at a faster rate than had been thought.","answer":"indicating","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"This buys some time for Samsung to figure out how to reboot its mobile strategy. But its fundamental dilemma hasn't changed: Lacking a software ecosystem to ___ itself, it struggles to compete with Apple on the high end and Chinese producers on the low end.","answer":"differentiate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"At Walker Road Primary School pupils speak nothing but French in some subjects from their first day in class, and this is known as early partial ___ teaching.","answer":"immersion","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Vince Cable has ___ to revitalise Britain's high streets by slashing the red tape that is preventing the development of new stores and offices.","answer":"pledged","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cn-en-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 6 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"跨越地中海的移民倾向于前往德国或瑞典。无论如何，法国和英国都不会站在欧洲移民浪潮压力下的前沿。(conceivable)","answer":"Migrants crossing the Mediterranean are more likely to head for countries like Germany or Sweden. By no conceivable measure is either France or Britain on the front line of Europe's migration crisis.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Fiorina女士认为多数中国公司并未掌握尖端技术，这是对的，但她以为中国公司不具备革新增值的能力，这是错的。(cutting edge)","answer":"Ms Fiorina is right that most Chinese firms are not at the cutting-edge of technology, but she is wrong to say they are incapable of value-creating innovation.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"斯坦福大学的经济学家Bob Hall认为，理论上讲，下一次衰退即将到来。不过，与人类不同，经济增长的寿终并非由于年头太长，而是由于不可预测的突发事件。(around the corner)","answer":"The next recession could in theory be around the corner. But unlike people, business expansions don't die of old age: they are killed by an unpredictable shock, says Bob Hall, an economist at Stanford University.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"政客们期望更多地攫取跨国公司所掌握的权益，包括公司手中八千万个工作机会和大约一万亿美元的利润。跨国公司依赖技术服务大赚特赚的同时，也就更容易遭受反击。(susceptible, backlash)","answer":"Politicians want to grab more of what multinational firms have come to control, including 80m jobs on their payrolls and their profits of about $1trn. As multinational firms come to make ever more of their money from technology services they become yet more susceptible to a backlash.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"除了上市公司之外，另一种最有趣的公司就是颇有潜力的新型创业公司，名字常常是稀奇古怪的unicorn和gazelles之类。数以千计的年轻人在租用的办公室里，借着咖啡和梦想作动力，琢磨创建新公司。(exotic, fuel)","answer":"But the most interesting alternative to public companies is a new breed of high-potential startups that go by exotic names such as unicorns and gazelles. Thousands of young people are creating new firms in temporary office spaces, fuelled by coffee and dreams.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-en-cn-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 6 英译汉（智能城市）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"A smart city happens when three specific networks interact: the communications grid, the energy system and the so-called \"logistics Internet\" — which can track people and things through transport and supply systems. But there is a problem: who controls the project and who owns the data it generates? We live in an age when your supermarket's software knows who you are from your buying choices; where your email provider can send you advertisements matched to key words in your supposedly private messages. But issues raised by smart cities go beyond privacy — they raise problems of liberty and control.","answer":"智能城市需由三个具体的互动网络组成：通讯网络、能源供应网络和所谓的\"物流网络\"，即能够通过运输和传送跟踪人和物的体系。然后问题就出来了：谁来控制智能城市系统，谁来拥有该系统所产生的数据？我们生活在一个超市软件能通过你的购买选择了解你是谁的时代，生活在一个电邮服务商能从你自以为私密的邮件中找到关键词并据此向你推出广告的时代，但是智能城市带来的问题超出了隐私话题的层次——这是关于自由和控制的问题。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-1-cloze-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 6 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["in","between","from","to","on","out","on","by","up","on"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The new network of things is already turning ___ to be very useful.","answer":"out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Smart cars are able to read emails and text messages to drivers ___ the move;","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"smart medical devices allow doctors to monitor patients ___ afar;","answer":"from","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Entire cities in South Korea are already rushing to link their infrastructure ___ the web to make it more efficient and improve services.","answer":"to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"\"There is a big difference ___ the Internet of things and other security issues,\"","answer":"between","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"says Joshua Corman of I Am The Cavalry, a group of security specialists trying to promote greater awareness of emerging risks ___ public safety.","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"\"If my PC is hit ___ a cyber-attack, it is a nuisance; if my car is attacked, it could kill me.\"","answer":"by","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Many items, including ordinary things like light bulbs and door locks, are being hooked ___ to the Internet by putting tiny computers into them and adding wireless connectivity.","answer":"up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The margins on them are wafer-thin, so manufacturers have little scope for spending ___ security.","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"And the systems are being produced in vast quantities, so hackers finding a flaw ___ one will be able to get into many others too.","answer":"in","type":"text","module":"Box"}]}]},{"key":"shangying-2","name":"商英教程2","units":[{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["perceive (n. perception; adj. perceptive; adv. perceptively)","articulate (n. articulateness; adj. articulate; adv. articulately)","condescend (n. condescension; adj. condescending; adv. condescendingly)","vibrate (n. vibration; adj. vibrant; adv. vibrantly)","elastic (n. elasticity; v. elasticize; adv. elastically)","exaggerate (n. exaggeration; adj. exaggerating/exaggerated; adv. exaggeratingly/exaggeratedly)","encroach (n. encroachment; adj. encroaching; adv. encroachingly)","synthesize (n. synthesis; adj. synthetic; adv. synthetically)","accommodate (n. accommodation; adj. accommodating; adv. accommodatingly)","globalize (n. globalization; adj. global; adv. globally)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Be careful to ___ your words so that everyone in the room can understand you.","answer":"articulate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"They were impressed by the student's ___ comment on the economic decline at the time.","answer":"perceptive","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"More diverse views can produce a more ___ society, but they may also split and weaken us.","answer":"vibrant","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"There is no escape from ___ warming — in the world today we have \"equality in adversity\".","answer":"global","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Some readers find that by talking about their reading with friends or fellow students, they are able to effectively ___ the material.","answer":"synthesize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"The definition of nationality is ___ in this cosmopolitan country.","answer":"elastic","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"It is said that we are too often ___ and imperialistic, seeking only to expand our power at the expense of others.","answer":"condescending","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Some people said they were struggling to balance their concern over the virus with what they saw as media ___ of the threat.","answer":"exaggeration","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Scientists worry that the warming climate will ___ on penguin habitats, threatening their populations across Antarctica.","answer":"encroach","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"The runway of this airport is undergoing expansion to ___ large planes.","answer":"accommodate","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 1 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"They are concerned ___ the training curriculum, but not the details of each course.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"I must brush ___ my English before I go to London.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"The problem, however, is that this bad habit can erode dental work, damaging your teeth and making them more susceptible ___ cavities.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"This building is ___ jeopardy of collapsing if there is a major earthquake.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"They are far ___ alone in being tempted to enter the property market rather than investing in expanding their own businesses.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"The composer transformed a simple folk tune ___ a complex set of variations.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"___ the whole, I would say that the performance was good, but certainly not great.","answer":"On","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"His father stared in surprise and then burst ___ tears.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"When the laws are not sufficiently respected, respect for the facts is bound ___ be insufficient, too.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Whatever you do ___ the start of the day sets the mood for the rest of the day.","answer":"at","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["bizarre","elasticity","go into effect","go out of business","paradoxically","umpteen","be concerned with","brush up","burst out (doing)","in jeopardy","tune into","complacent","ludicrously","polymath","susceptible to","burst out","went into effect","was concerned with"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"If you weren't so ___ you could change things for the better.","answer":"complacent","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"On hearing the bad news, Mary ___ crying.","answer":"burst out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"A trademark law and a patent law had been promulgated and put in force. On June 1, 1991, a copyright law ___.","answer":"went into effect","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"To our surprise, he showed up at the press conference in a most ___ outfit.","answer":"bizarre","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The most successful corporate brands are universal and so ___ facilitate differences of interpretation that appeal to different groups.","answer":"paradoxically","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Are they \"bored\" because they have been to the parade and seen it ___ times on TV?","answer":"umpteen","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Tim Parks is a(n) ___ among authors: a prolific novelist, translator, essayist and memoirist, as well as an authoritative writer about football.","answer":"polymath","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"This is Susan Block. ___ Date Night next week; same time, same station, for another Saturday night on Date Night.","answer":"Tune into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"I must ___ my French before I go to Paris.","answer":"brush up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"What other traditions do you think are also ___ to be lost? Maybe something about family, marriage, individual, work, money, or parents?","answer":"in jeopardy","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"Although apparently rigid, bones exhibit a degree of ___ that enables the skeleton to withstand considerable impact.","answer":"elasticity","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"At that time George ___ money and power exclusively.","answer":"was concerned with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"The evening dress with artificial crystals is ___ expensive.","answer":"ludicrously","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"We need to cut costs quickly, or we will ___.","answer":"go out of business","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The young revolutionaries were ___ propaganda.","answer":"susceptible to","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 1 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"到了三十年代，这里有众多的画廊，数量是二十年代的两倍，而且电影院比世界上任何其他城市都多。（galore, as many again as）","answer":"By the thirties there were picture-halls galore, as many again as in the twenties, and with more cinemas than any other city in the world.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"如果未来一年之内我们不能适应市场的快速变化并招揽更多的顾客，公司可能会面临倒闭。（accommodate, go out of business）","answer":"If we cannot accommodate the rapid changes in the market and get more customers in the next year, our company will go out of business.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"人们驱使自己不断进步，是因为他们不想做自己，而渴望像那些更“酷”、更“优秀”的人一样去经历人生。（be driven to, aspire to do）","answer":"People are driven to improve because they want to escape the experience of being themselves; instead they aspire to experience life as someone who's \"cooler\" or \"better\" than they are.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"复杂的革新型金融体系固然容易带来破坏性疯长，但是单一、严格管制的金融体系势必导致经济发展迟缓。（susceptible, regulate）","answer":"A sophisticated and innovative financial system is susceptible to destructive booms; but a simple, tightly regulated one will condemn an economy to grow slow.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"布什总统说远远不止他一人担心美国未来经济的发展，持续不稳定的房地产市场可能使更多人面临失业和危险。（far from alone, in jeopardy）","answer":"President Bush says he is far from alone to be concerned about the future of American economy, with the risk that continued instability in the housing market could put more jobs in jeopardy.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 1 英译汉（翻译耳机）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It has been a staple of science fiction for decades, and could be a godsend for tourists grappling with directions to their hotel. An earpiece that lets its wearer understand other nationalities by instantly translating foreign languages is due to go on sale next month. The £140 device, which can decode eight languages, is inspired by translators such as the Babel fish from The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, which allowed the earthling Arthur Dent to comprehend alien races on his adventures. Lingmo International, the Australian firm behind the Translate One2One earpiece, said it would put an end to awkward international meetings between politicians and business leaders. The device translates sentences in three to five seconds using IBM's artificial intelligence language software, Watson. It is the first earpiece of its kind to translate languages without needing a constant connection to a mobile phone or Wi-Fi signal, and can translate between English, French, Italian, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese, German and Chinese. There is one catch, however: the speaker and listener will have to wear a device each for the translation software to work. Several technology companies are developing language earpieces aimed at making embarrassing holiday encounters a thing of the past, while Google recently upgraded its translation software so that it is able to understand full sentences, instead of converting phrases word by word.","answer":"它是几十年来科幻小说的主题，也可能会成为在去宾馆途中迷路的游客们的福音。一款可以即时翻译外国语言、让佩戴者听懂外国人说话的耳机将于下月开始发售。这款耳机售价140英镑，可以翻译八种语言，它是受到《银河系漫游指南》中巴别鱼等“翻译员”的启发制成的，巴别鱼让地球人阿瑟·邓特能在探险中听懂外星人的语言。这款“翻译一对一”耳机是澳大利亚公司Lingmo International开发的，该公司表示这款耳机将结束政界人士和商业领袖出席国际会议时的尴尬。它使用IBM公司的人工智能语言软件Watson，能在三至五秒的时间里翻译出语句。这是首款无需一直连接到手机或无线网络信号就能翻译语言的耳机，可翻译的语言包括英语、法语、意大利语、西班牙语、巴西葡萄牙语、德语和汉语。但有一点：讲话者和倾听者都需要佩戴耳机，翻译软件才能工作。目前有多家科技公司都在研发语言翻译耳机，以使尴尬的假日邂逅成为历史。谷歌公司近日也对其翻译软件进行了升级，使其可以理解全句，而不再逐词转换短语。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 1 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["globalization","jeopardy","accommodated","manifests","elasticity","encroachment","multilingualism","debilitating","susceptible to","entry","lingua franca","tune into","gone into effect","multinationalism","integration"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"With the advent of economic ___, English looms growingly large in international trade and cultural communication, serving as a shared language.","answer":"globalization","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Despite the ___ to the world market gained from the accommodation to English, many countries have found their local cultures are in jeopardy.","answer":"entry","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Despite the entry to the world market gained from the accommodation to English, many countries have found their local cultures are in ___.","answer":"jeopardy","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"With the ___ of English, the native culture is also susceptible to change.","answer":"encroachment","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"With the encroachment of English, the native culture is also ___ change.","answer":"susceptible to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"In some countries, laws have ___ to oblige the use of native language in promotion of foreign products.","answer":"gone into effect","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Paradoxically, along with the process of homogenization, ___ becomes an equally noteworthy trend.","answer":"multilingualism","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Owing to its multi-origins as well as its contact with different languages, English also ___ considerable elasticity.","answer":"manifests","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"Owing to its multi-origins as well as its contact with different languages, English also manifests considerable ___.","answer":"elasticity","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and has ___ to other languages and regional English dialects.","answer":"accommodated","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["accuse (n. accusation; adj. accusatory; adv. accusatorily)","priority (v. prioritize; adj. prior; adv. priorly)","diversity (v. diversify; adj. diverse; adv. diversely)","constitution (v. constitute; adj. constitutive; adv. constitutively)","intrusion (v. intrude; adj. intrusive; adv. intrusively)","perception (v. perceive; adj. perceptive; adv. perceptively)","competency (v. compete; adj. competent; adv. competently)","affection (v. affect; adj. affective; adv. affectively)","cultivation (v. cultivate; adj. cultivated)","devastation (v. devastate; adj. devastating; adv. devastatingly)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The economists believe that societies ___ crops like wheat and barley may have experienced extra pressure to protect their harvests.","answer":"cultivating","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"We have to call people \"him\" and \"her\" even if we believe that people's genders are determined by their biological sex and not by their self-___ , which, by the way, can rapidly change, for those who are \"gender-fluid\".","answer":"perception","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"The company is fully ___ and able to guarantee customers the product design and processing quality.","answer":"competent","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"You can only use the books on this shelf with ___ agreement.","answer":"prior","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Her assistant was ___ of theft and fraud by the police.","answer":"accused","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"FERC's actions were challenged by electricity generators, who said that the commission could only regulate wholesale sales of electricity and that its ___ program on the retail market, which is the exclusive province of state regulators.","answer":"intruded","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"It will be a(n) ___ blow for the city if the automobile factories close.","answer":"devastating","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"The government will unveil a new rule that would ___ millions of middle-income workers eligible for overtime pay.","answer":"affect","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"You should invest wisely and ___ your portfolios.","answer":"diversify","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"In order to ___ the offence of business conspiracy, there is no need to establish that the object of the conspiracy was, in fact, carried out; the offence is established at the time of the agreement between competitors to engage in the conduct.","answer":"constitute","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 2 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The photographer was ___ assignment for Life magazine, for a story on romance in Paris, and hired the couple as models for the shot.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"I will not fail ___ my mission to raise our daughters in a loving and peaceful family, even if this means leaving you to raise them and support them entirely on my own.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Clearly, this trend of supply chain management has set higher requirements ___ the conduct of integration.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Alternative payment companies entice buyers who may not have credit cards, feel wary ___ sharing their information online or just want an easier checkout experience.","answer":"about","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The funds' partners — donor countries, funding recipients, and five multilateral development banks — are meeting in Washington this week to take stock ___ progress toward these goals.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"With a larger pool of available resources, companies can staff projects more efficiently and draw ___ talents from many sites.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Either we explode with rage or bottle our emotions, turning ___ angry harms ourselves, which sometimes ends up with feelings of depression.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"The market has reacted negatively throughout the year to any moves that are perceived ___ an effort to slow down the economy.","answer":"as","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"The enterprise methodologies and frameworks that exist today vary ___ significantly the range of problems they solve and the approaches they take.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"The strength of the dollar, the pace of growth in China, politics in Iran, instability in the Middle East, new finds, OPEC decisions and more play ___ the ultimate price of oil.","answer":"Into","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["subsidiary","subordinate","counterpart","confrontational","delegate","preliminary","bargain","proceed","implicit","take stock of","intricacy","disseminate","hierarchical","incentive","viable","disseminating","counterparts","delegated","Incentives"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"A new study analyzing how social norms are perpetuated within the Wikipedia community says they look a lot like a corporate bureaucracy, with a(n) ___ structure of power.","answer":"hierarchical","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The Supreme Court ruled Monday that a man who sued a digital company ___ for inaccurate information about him must do more to show he was actually harmed by the mistakes.","answer":"disseminating","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Former lightweight boxing champ Paul Spadafora faces a(n) ___ hearing on charges that he put a woman in a semi-headlock at a Pittsburgh-area bar, drank some of her beer and then threw her to the ground when she went outside to call police.","answer":"preliminary","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"In 2007, Vodafone, one of the world's biggest telecom providers, moved to buy Hutchison Essar Ltd, an Indian ___ of a Hong Kong SAR-based company.","answer":"subsidiary","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The new president will have to ___ with the trade pact signed by his predecessor.","answer":"proceed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"The equity lender may refuse to ___ its position to the new lender.","answer":"subordinate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Looking at temperatures and the extent of sea ice are surely the most obvious ways to ___ what's happening in the Arctic.","answer":"take stock of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"I don't believe the employees will like a(n) ___ style of management.","answer":"confrontational","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"White-Hispanics and white-other daters were less willing to state a preference to date Asians compared to their black-Hispanic ___.","answer":"counterparts","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"The new manager was ___ to reorganize the department.","answer":"delegated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"Nissan Chief Executive Carlos Ghosn is confident that a 237 billion yen ($2.2 billion) investment in a controlling stake in scandal-embroiled Mitsubishi Motors will prove a(n) ___ when sheer size is critical in the auto industry.","answer":"bargain","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"___ biases — those unconscious assumptions that worm their way into our brains, without our full awareness and sometimes against our better judgment — can influence grading choices from teachers, split-second decisions by police officers and outcomes in online dating.","answer":"Implicit","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"With a degree in Physiology & Developmental Biology, I have gained a deep understanding of the human body and appreciate the ___ of life.","answer":"intricacy","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Baltimore Ravens' offensive tackle Eugene Monroe is on a mission to remove marijuana from the NFL's banned substance list, hoping that the NFL will recognize cannabis as a(n) ___ treatment option.","answer":"viable","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Norway has used government ___ and subsidies to prompt electronic vehicle (EV) purchases — offsetting the relatively high cost of the vehicle.","answer":"Incentives","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 2 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"鉴于目前文化节目同质化严重的趋势，有关部门高度重视，给予原创节目财务和政策上的激励。（homogeneity, incentive, priority）","answer":"Given the worsening condition of homogeneity among cultural programs, relevant governmental agencies have attached high priority to original programs by offering financial and policy incentives.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"长期以来，将无限度的捐赠和信息完全公开结合的简单策略为竞选活动财政中不可调和的问题提供了得当的解决方法。（finesse, irreconcilable）","answer":"For a long time, the simple finesse of coupling unlimited donations and full disclosure offered a rather elegant solution to the irreconcilables of campaign finance.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"在美国，美食仍然存在一种隐性的、内部的层级结构，你都无法想象人们愿意为那些所谓享有盛名的食物花多少钱。（implicit hierarchy, prestigious）","answer":"In the United States, there is still an implicit and internal hierarchy of food/taste. You could hardly imagine how much people are willing to pay for those so-called prestigious cuisines.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"我们想找一个快速发布信息、没有中间环节也不受繁琐手续制约的平台。（disseminate, intermediary, circumvent）","answer":"We are looking for a platform where we could disseminate the message quickly, without any kind of intermediary, and can circumvent any red tape.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"没有人认为纽约式的言谈举止招人喜欢或高贵，但他们的确是能力、进取和率直的体现。（perceive, demeanor, competence）","answer":"People do not perceive the New York style of speaking and demeanor as particularly attractive or high-status. But they do associate them with competence, aggressiveness and directness.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 2 英译汉（谈判风格）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Westerners tend to stress process when making decisions. Their emphasis on process encourages them to develop what are known as \"fair play rules\", rules about procedures that assure that decisions will be made fairly. They also expect others to be as concerned about following the rules as they are. Sometimes Westerners are described as legalistic, meaning that they expect people to follow precise rules contained in laws, contracts, and agreements. People from high context, collectivist cultures are more likely to be concerned about relationships (in-groups and out-groups) and status than about particular rules. These differences influence the negotiation strategies used by each side. Westerners think negotiations progress when the parties get down to work on specific details. A good relationship comes from reaching agreement on many specific items. A Western negotiating team may begin by enthusiastically promoting their ideal position as to how the details can be worked out, then gradually pull back through a series of compromises to whatever positions the Chinese negotiators are willing to accept. Chinese negotiators usually avoid discussing details in the early phase of negotiations. Instead they discuss mutual interest and general principles. When the Westerners commit themselves to these (a commitment that the Westerners may not take very seriously because of the lack of details), Chinese negotiators will appeal to those mutual interests to get the other side to agree to what the details should be.","answer":"西方人一般会强调决策的过程，对过程的重视促使他们建立公平的游戏规则，即确保决策公平的各步骤规则。他们也期待他人同样注重规则的遵守。有时候人们称西方人为拘泥于法律条文的人，就是说他们想让大家都严格遵守法律、合同、协议中的条条框框。来自高语境、集体主义文化的人们则更关注关系（个人所属的团体和他人团体）和地位，这些都超过了他们对某条规则的关注。这些差异影响了各方在谈判时采取的策略。西方人认为双方商讨特定细节是谈判获得进展的标志。良好的关系来自就特定细节达成的一致。谈判组一开始就会热切地陈述他们理想中的立场，如何解决细节问题，然后根据中国谈判对手愿意接受的条件而逐渐作出一系列妥协。中国谈判者在初始阶段一般会避开对细节的讨论，而交流共同的利益和总体原则。当西方人表示愿意接受这些时（他们并非当真接受，因为缺少细节），中方谈判者会借此互利原则要求对方接受他们的具体条件。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 2 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words given in the box. Some words will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["accuse","basis","blurry","conspiracy","content","disputes","expand","immunity","invest","manage","private","reconcile","record","shelter","tough"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"U.S. companies have found it can be ___ to do business in China.","answer":"tough","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Now, as more Chinese firms ___ in the United States, they're finding it can be hard to reconcile with Chinese companies on American turf, too.","answer":"invest","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Now, as more Chinese firms invest in the United States, they're finding it can be hard to ___ with Chinese companies on American turf, too.","answer":"reconcile","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"They have different understanding of business practices from U.S. companies' because they are on different cultural ___.","answer":"basis","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"___ are destined to grow as Chinese companies invest more in the United States and sign more contracts on U.S. shores.","answer":"Disputes","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"China's investment in the United States reached a(n) ___ $15.7 billion in 2015.","answer":"record","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"These conflicts are complicated by the ___ concept of public and private in the Chinese culture.","answer":"blurry","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"These conflicts are complicated by the blurry concept of public and ___ in the Chinese culture.","answer":"private","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"As Chinese companies increasingly ___ internationally, both sides will need to manage cultural differences in order to reach win-win results.","answer":"expand","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"As Chinese companies increasingly expand internationally, both sides will need to ___ cultural differences in order to reach win-win results in communication with companies from across the Pacific Ocean.","answer":"manage","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["energy (adj. energetic; adv. energetically)","prestige (adj. prestigious)","compel (n. compulsion; adj. compulsory)","ambiguous (n. ambiguity; adv. ambiguously)","commit (n. commitment)","supreme (n. supremacy; adv. supremely)","justify (n. justification; adj. justified)","imagine (n. imagination; adj. imaginative)","sustain (n. sustenance; adj. sustainable/sustained; adv. sustainably)","provoke (n. provocation; adj. provocative)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Everyone told her she looked very handsome, and she was in a spirited and ___ mood unusual with her.","answer":"energetic","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"His ___ has been raised greatly since he was promoted to the president of the university.","answer":"prestige","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Primary instruction is free but not ___ , and the schools are supported and supervised by the states.","answer":"compulsory","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"The ending was more ___ , one in which the future of the world was in question.","answer":"ambiguous","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"As part of this ___ to infrastructure, we need to upgrade our digital super highway as well.","answer":"commitment","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"The ability to write is a(n) ___ test of linguistic competence.","answer":"supreme","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"He did the dishes as well, hoping for an early reprieve from her ___ anger.","answer":"justified","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"___ is not only the uniquely human capacity to envision that which is not, and therefore the fount of all invention and innovation.","answer":"Imagination","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Biodiversity ___ conservation in agriculture not only relates to the development of agriculture, but also is an essential part of species conservation.","answer":"sustainable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"French patriotic feeling, suspicious, angry and alarmed, needed only a slight ___ to cause it to blaze up into an uncontrollable fever for war.","answer":"provocation","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 3 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"He noticed how a beam would enter the milk and scatter reasonably uniformly ___ the material.","answer":"through","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"By reading the following test data, you can see how we arrived at our results and evaluate whether or not the findings apply ___ your environment.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"They include such traits as integrity, honesty, courage, fairness and generosity which arise ___ the hard choices we have to make in life.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"She found that he spent almost all of his time at work and at the bars, having grown accustomed ___ a life without her there.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The stereotype of German humourlessness is believed to derive ___ their reputation for efficiency, punctuality and rationality, presumed to be at the expense of humour.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Never make false promises: a child, even tiny, develops confidence in her parents and they must remain consistent ___ their actions and their words.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"In a news conference late Tuesday, developing countries demanded rich countries commit ___ a 40-percent overall cut on emissions.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Whether at work or at home, the goal is to engage ___ activities that are both personally significant and enjoyable.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"In the process we draw ___ the expertise of outsiders and the fresh ideas of our new recruits.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"It is only in marriage with the world that our ideals can bear fruit; divorced ___ it, they remain barren.","answer":"from","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["apply to","arise from","be divorced from","in terms of","consist in","derive from","elicit","draw on","grapple with","no matter what","be accustomed to","articulate","commit to","pose","reconcile","poses","committed ... to","accustomed to","arose ... from","grappled with","applied to","draws ... on","divorced from","consists in"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The increase in student numbers ___ many problems for the universities.","answer":"poses","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Since the couple could not ___ their differences, they decided to get a divorce.","answer":"reconcile","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Bill Gates has ___ himself ___ working for the public good after retirement.","answer":"committed ... to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Many developers are working individually, ___ spending most of their time reading specifications, working through designs, and coding.","answer":"accustomed to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"His illness partly ___ want of food.","answer":"arose ... from","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Sometimes people have emotions that they find difficult to ___.","answer":"articulate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"It is high time that the government ___ the ever-growing unemployment in the country.","answer":"grappled with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"We are prone to interpret the actions of children ___ our own experience.","answer":"in terms of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"By patient questioning we managed to ___ enough information from the witnesses.","answer":"elicit","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Scientific discoveries are often ___ industrial production methods.","answer":"applied to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"We should be judged by the quality of our products and the value investors ___ them.","answer":"derive from","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"His book heavily ___ his experiences abroad.","answer":"draws ... on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"His hopes for the future are often completely ___ reality.","answer":"divorced from","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Cooperation ___ helping one another and sharing losses and gains.","answer":"consists in","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"My parents always waited up for me ___ I got home.","answer":"no matter what","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 3 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"除了永不满足的好奇心，理查德·布兰森还以冒险精神和对生活的热情而闻名，这使他成为全球最受钦佩的企业家之一，因为他能很好地平衡工作与生活。（apart from, zest）","answer":"Apart from the insatiable curiosity, Richard Branson is also famous for his spirit of adventure and zest for life, which makes him one of the most admired entrepreneurs globally for his ability to have a successful work-life balance.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"教育就是获得利用知识的艺术。大学的作用是让学生摆脱细节，选择基本原理。（acquisition, in favor of）","answer":"Education is the acquisition of the art of utilizing knowledge. The function of a university is to enable students to shed details in favor of general principles.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"哈佛商学院首创了“案例教学法”，学生通过这种方法对一家公司在真实商业环境中遇到的困境进行评估和讨论。（encounter, evaluate, pioneer）","answer":"The Harvard Business School pioneered the \"case method\", with which students evaluate and debate a dilemma a company encountered in real business situations.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"从财务主管转为商学院讲师并不总是那么容易。对于由首席财务官转行的讲师来说，有一些先决条件：在业内要有良好的声誉，善于与人相处，最重要的是能够与学生打成一片。（engage, prerequisites, transition）","answer":"The transition from finance chief to business-school lecturer isn't always easy. There are some prerequisites for CFOs-turned-lecturers. It's important to have an excellent reputation in the field, be good with people and, most importantly, be able to engage with students.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"但你们中的许多人现在都在想，这些责任如何与职业选择相匹配。有必要在报酬丰厚的工作和有意义的工作之间做出选择吗？如果只能二选一，你会怎么选？有没有两全其美的办法？（commitment, remunerative）","answer":"But many of you are now wondering how these commitments fit with a career choice. Is it necessary to decide between remunerative work and meaningful work? If it were to be either/or, which would you choose? Is there a way to have both?","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 3 英译汉（随身摄像头）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Teachers in UK schools are trialling the use of body cameras in class to record bad pupils' behaviour, it has been revealed. At least two schools in England have introduced the equipment for constant recording with the consent of local education authorities. The cameras, worn on teachers' clothing, are set to film all the time but only save encrypted footage when the record button is pressed, The Times reported. Teachers are advised to turn on the cameras during incidents in the classroom to tackle \"constant low-level disruption\", but must give notice before doing so. Footage could also be shared with parents to involve them in addressing their children's behaviour. Feedback from parents and schools was said to be positive, with teachers praising them as an effective deterrent.","answer":"据悉，英国学校的教师正在尝试在课堂上使用随身摄像头，记录表现差的孩子的行为。英格兰至少有两家学校已经引进了这种设备进行持续录像，这已经得到了当地教育部门的同意。《泰晤士报》报道说，这种摄像头戴在教师的衣服上，可以一直录像，但只有按下录像按钮时，才会保存下加密影像。校方建议老师在课堂上出现麻烦时打开摄像头，以处理“不间断的小打小闹”，但在打开摄像头前必须告知大家。家长也会得到这些影像资料，以便他们参与处理孩子的行为。从家长和学校那里得到的关于安置摄像头的反馈据说是积极的，很多老师认为这是有效的威慑手段。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 3 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words given in the box. Some words will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["another","also","both","But","either","for","however","nor","not","or","thought","while","with","yet"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It's one thing to brag on a website about brilliant faculty. It's ___ when tens of thousands of people experience their brilliance firsthand, with the college's name attached.","answer":"another","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"It's another when tens of thousands of people experience their brilliance firsthand, ___ the college's name attached.","answer":"with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The vast enrollments that provide these benefits — the sharing of knowledge, feedback from huge numbers of students, widespread publicity — ___ create problems.","answer":"also","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"___ professors have found ways to promote discussions and collaborative learning among students, we have not yet figured out how to monitor exams to protect against cheating or plagiarism.","answer":"While","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"While professors have found ways to promote discussions and collaborative learning among students, we have not ___ figured out how to monitor exams to protect against cheating or plagiarism.","answer":"yet","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"how to answer students' questions, ___ how to identify and assist those who are struggling.","answer":"or","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Successful MOOC participants are self-motivated and hold themselves accountable for watching lectures, completing coursework, and fulfilling all requirements. ___ they are also rare: the completion rate for the first MOOC, a course on artificial intelligence offered by Stanford in 2011, was 13 percent.","answer":"But","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"___ have universities crafted a viable business model for MOOCs.","answer":"Nor","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"___ a fee Coursera provides potential employers with the names of high-achieving students.","answer":"For","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"In ___ cases some of the money is returned to participating institutions, but, at present, it is insufficient to cover the costs of course development.","answer":"both","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["acquire (n. acquisition/acquisitiveness; adj. acquisitive; adv. acquisitively)","contemplate (n. contemplation; adj. contemplative)","dissipate (n. dissipation; adj. dissipated)","suspect (n. suspicion; adj. suspicious; adv. suspiciously)","averse (n. aversion; adv. aversely)","succeed (n. succession/success; adj. successive; adv. successively)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The company has made ___ of land in several Asian countries since the ambitious new CEO assumed office.","answer":"acquisitions","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"As we ___ whether we absolutely must end war, we should consider how life lived on a war footing affects our most basic rights and freedom.","answer":"contemplate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"His youth was passed in scandalous ___ , which drew upon himself and his coterie the detestation of the people of Paris.","answer":"dissipation","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"Fair-minded people declined to condemn her on mere ___ , and so the injurious talk made no very damaging headway.","answer":"suspicion","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"His most severe measures were taken in cold blood, as part of his general policy; but his natural disposition was to ___ unnecessary bloodshed or cruelty.","answer":"averse","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"All these questions roused a tumult of unprecedented violence in her young, ardent, inexperienced soul, which was renewed each ___ night.","answer":"successive","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"He made a French gesture, a shrug of his thin shoulders, which caused me to ___ he was not always so good-natured.","answer":"suspect","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Those were his most hard-working days. One novel ___ to another during the ten years.","answer":"succeeded","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Jack slanted his eye up at the Doctor, as if he was getting ___ some kind of advantage over him.","answer":"suspiciously","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"They are ___ of money; you can never satisfy them.","answer":"acquisitive","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 4 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Many of the soldiers had to subsist ___ insects and roots.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Mortgage rates tumbled ___ their lowest level for 25 years.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Her shoulders shook, her mouth compressed; she knotted her fingers and squeezed the blood ___ of them.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Why don't you scatter a few cushions ___ the room?","answer":"around","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"Higher inflation rates have already had a major impact ___ spending.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"He was in dispute ___ the company about his contract.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Each barrel of oil is equivalent ___ about 40 gallons of gasoline.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"He's never had to grapple ___ the issues that most principals deal with.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"My love of law is almost equal to my aversion ___ lawyers.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"His explanation sounds fairly plausible ___ me.","answer":"to","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["astutely","wrestle","symbolism","far-flung","colossus","proliferate","subsist","punitive","incremental","pester","dissipate","transform","overhaul","topple","confront"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"What they can do is ___ with the fundamental questions that govern the fate of any enterprise.","answer":"wrestle","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Carriers could spare their wireless networks 20% to 40% of ___ traffic growth by offloading.","answer":"incremental","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"China's demand for oil, iron ore and other raw materials is pumping money into developing economies as ___ as Angola and Kazakhstan that supply them.","answer":"far-flung","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"As China becomes an economic ___ , its increasing appetite for scarce natural resources will inevitably extend to the world's most sought-after wines.","answer":"colossus","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"You ___ this uninteresting piece of domesticity into an ideal woman, ennobling her surroundings.","answer":"transform","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"While certainly not a pattern followed by extraordinary executives, many people have advanced their careers by playing internal politics ___.","answer":"astutely","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Both companies were the little guy once: Apple was David aiming his catapult at Microsoft, and Google was the second-mover hoping to ___ the might of Yahoo!","answer":"topple","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Japan recognizes the rise of China. As a warning shot in an intensifying rivalry, Tokyo last week put import tariffs on Chinese ___ steel.","answer":"punitive","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"To trace the gradual elaboration of the ___ and use of ceremonial lights in the Church, until its full development and systematization in the middle ages, would be impossible here.","answer":"symbolism","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"As social media and user-generated reviews ___ , the power of negative feedback will only increase — making it even more imperative that products be ready before they hit the market.","answer":"proliferate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"A religion could not permanently ___ in this world of space and time without some external concrete embodiment.","answer":"subsist","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"She reached the platform to ___ a group of upturned, staring faces, and for the moment her courage failed her.","answer":"confront","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Many people vocalized how the retailer only wanted their information to ___ them with marketing messages they didn't want.","answer":"pester","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"He believes that as well as looking for new forms of revenue on the web, newspapers should ___ their print editions to make themselves more relevant and thus boost circulation.","answer":"overhaul","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"A breath of air which made its way in through the open pane, helped to ___ the smell of the charcoal and to conceal the presence of the brazier.","answer":"dissipate","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 4 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"出于对新监狱看守的厌恶，这名囚犯花了两个月时间挖隧道逃出了那座臭名昭著、戒备森严的监狱。（motivate, aversion）","answer":"Motivated by aversion to the new prison guard, the prisoner spent two months tunneling his way out of the notorious and high-security (heavily guarded) prison.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"美国有适应这种新外交规则的灵活性、能力和领导力，但欧洲根本没有。（adapt to, leadership）","answer":"America has the flexibility, capacity, and leadership to adapt to the new rules of diplomacy, but Europe simply does not.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"尽管特蕾莎修女的工作受到如此多的关注和赞扬，她始终是一个极为谦逊的人。（humility, despite）","answer":"Mother Theresa remained a woman of great humility despite all the attention and praise for her work.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"如果我是你，我不会忽视这个障碍——竞争比你想象的更激烈，我们必须继续就我们关心的问题坦率而有力地发声。（overlook, fierce）","answer":"I wouldn't overlook the obstacle if I were you — the competition is more fierce than you think, we must continue to speak frankly and forcefully on issues that concern us.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"如今该地区的大多数人都只能靠很低的收入维持生计，因此这次自发的抗议是该国自2008年陷入经济衰退以来最大的一次。（subsist, spontaneous）","answer":"Nowadays most people in the region have to subsist on very low incomes, so this spontaneous protest is the largest since the country plunged into recession in 2008.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 4 英译汉（CEO的性格）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Getting up early, wearing the same clothes every day, eating eggs for breakfast ... there are various things we're told CEOs do that may hold the keys to their success. But what if the one thing the most successful have in common is in fact not something they do but the way they are? The results of a new study certainly suggest this is the case. And the shared attribute? Introversion. Researchers from ghSmart, a Chicago-based consultancy firm, spent ten years analysing the personalities of 2,000 CEOs and reached the conclusion that the majority of the successful ones were introverts. This flies in the face of the image most people have of a typical charismatic, confident, extroverted leader. The study, called the CEO Genome Project, includes a test anyone can do to find out whether they have what it takes to be a CEO. \"When we flip on the news, or check our social media feeds, we are bombarded with images of well-groomed, Ivy league-educated icons of the Fortune 100,\" the study authors write. \"And we can't help but think, I could never be them. In fact, they come from surprisingly varied backgrounds. Of the six million CEOs of companies in America, only seven percent went to an elite school — and eight percent didn't graduate from college at all. Some are immigrants; many worked their way up through the ranks from entry-level positions.\" To reach their conclusions, the researchers made a database of assessments, including comprehensive performance appraisals and extensive biographical information, which documented everything from behavioural patterns and demographic information to career history and previous job performance. From these findings, they were able to work out who amongst us are most likely to become CEOs. They found that the four most important traits for CEOs are: 1. Reaching out to stakeholders; 2. Being highly adaptable to change; 3. Being reliable and predictable rather than showing exceptional, and perhaps not repeatable, performance; 4. Making fast decisions with conviction, if not necessarily perfect ones. About half of the candidates had at least one of these characteristics.","answer":"早早起床，每天穿一样的衣服，早餐吃鸡蛋……人们告诉我们，首席执行官们做的这些五花八门的事情也许就是他们成功的关键。但有没有可能最成功的首席执行官的共同之处其实不是他们做的某件事，而是他们的性格呢？一项新研究的结果告诉我们，的确是这样。而他们共有的特点是什么？那就是内向。总部位于芝加哥的咨询公司ghSmart的研究人员花了10年时间分析2000位首席执行官的性格，得出结论：大部分成功者都是内向的人。在大多数人的眼中，领导都是魅力十足、自信满满的外向者，这项研究结果真是出人意料。这项研究名为“CEO基因组计划”，其中包括一项任何人都可以参与的测试，来发现他们是否有成为一名首席执行官的特质。研究报告的作者写道：“当我们浏览新闻，或者翻阅社交媒体信息时，看到的都是衣冠楚楚、常春藤盟校毕业、上榜财富100强的偶像。于是我们不禁认为，自己永远也成不了他们那样的人。事实上，他们的背景惊人地多样。在美国600万名公司首席执行官中，仅有7%曾在名校就读，还有8%压根就不是大学毕业生。有些人是移民，很多人是从基层岗位升上去的。”为得出结论，研究人员制作了评估数据库，包括综合绩效考察和大量的个人信息，其中的记录遍及方方面面，包括行为类型、人口统计信息、职业经历和以前的工作表现等等。从这些发现中，他们能找出我们当中哪些人最可能成为首席执行官。他们发现首席执行官的四种最重要的特点是：1. 愿意倾听股东的想法；2. 对变化有高度适应性；3. 可靠，行为可预见，而不是作出异常的、或许不可重复的表现；4. 有信念，决断快，尽管他们的决策并不全都无懈可击。大约半数被调查者至少具有上述一种特点。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 4 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words given in the box. Some words will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["join","of","on","profoundly","relatively","same","take","while","with","yet"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"___ so much of our lives have changed profoundly as a result of our living in the Internet Era, there has been relatively little impact on the way we organize the ways we work.","answer":"While","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"While so much of our lives have changed ___ as a result of our living in the Internet Era, there has been relatively little impact on the way we organize the ways we work.","answer":"profoundly","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"While so much of our lives have changed profoundly as a result of our living in the Internet Era, there has been ___ little impact on the way we organize the ways we work.","answer":"relatively","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Our dreams and capabilities have been profoundly altered by real-time ___ to ubiquitous information, and abundant choices, but our work methods have shared little of this magic.","answer":"access","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Mr. Zhang has embarked ___ an experiment to reinvent Haier, yet again, by breaking down the corporate walls and the way it has organized in the past.","answer":"on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Mr. Zhang has embarked on an experiment to reinvent Haier, ___ again, by breaking down the corporate walls and the way it has organized in the past, and positioning it as a platform where others can join in to pursue their dreams.","answer":"yet","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"and positioning it ___ a platform where others can join in to pursue their dreams with Haiers existing assets and talent","answer":"as","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"and positioning it as a platform where others can join in to pursue their dreams ___ Haiers existing assets and talent, much the same way as Apple has provided us with a mass-produced device (iPhones or iPads) and invited app developers to join in to create the magic of those experiences.","answer":"with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"much the ___ way as Apple has provided us with a mass-produced device (iPhones or iPads) and invited app developers to join in to create the magic of those experiences.","answer":"same","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and invited app developers to ___ in to create the magic of those experiences.","answer":"join","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["amass (v. amass; n. amassment)","ego (n. ego/egotism; adj. egotistical; adv. egotistically)","prevalent (n. prevalence; adv. prevalently)","dispense (n. dispensation; adj. dispensable)","acquire (n. acquisition; adj. acquisitive)","disrupt (n. disruption; adj. disruptive; adv. disruptively)","characterize (n. character; adj. characteristic)","exceed (n. excess; adj. excessive; adv. excessively)","dismiss (n. dismissal; adj. dismissive)","participate (n. participation; adj. participatory)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Some people envy the enormous wealth that J. K. Rowling has ___ from her Harry Potter series.","answer":"amassed","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Compared with the philanthropic act of the world No. 1 billionaire, he has been perceived as ___ showy.","answer":"egotistically","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"More and more people have come to realize the ___ of English and want to have a command of it.","answer":"prevalence","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"You can contact this famous nongovernmental organization for the ___ of relief to the war-inflicted refugees.","answer":"dispensation","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"I like your earrings — are they a recent ___?","answer":"acquisition","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"The naughty boy is a headache for the teacher because he is a noisy, ___ influence in class.","answer":"disruptive","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"The modern cities are all ___ by skyscrapers with steel and glass.","answer":"characterized","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"A lot of people are suffering from a(n) ___ of stress in modern times.","answer":"excess","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Two agents got their ___ this morning for having taken bribery and engaged in inside trading.","answer":"dismissals","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"The company adopts a(n) ___ style of management in which the staff are encouraged to get involved in its decision-making.","answer":"participatory","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 5 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The teacher said the girl's success lies ___ her keen appetite ___ knowledge rather than her aptitude.","answer":"in ... for","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"A visionary leader with penetrating insight together with a group of followers with team spirit make ___ an efficient and successful team.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"The legendary diamond Blue Belle of Asia will be put ___ auction again this November.","answer":"up for","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Many people doubt Donald Trump's being elected American president can usher ___ a new era for American politics.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"With so many means available to beautify a person now, a homely face can be transformed ___ a radiant star face.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"The timely business trip helped him get ___ the dilemma whether to attend the birthday celebration of a senior he disliked.","answer":"round","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"I hope I can do something for you ___ return ___ your hospitality and help extended to me during my visit here.","answer":"in ... for","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Firms have to adopt \"inflation accounting\" techniques in which all costs, revenues, profits and losses are fully adjusted ___ inflation.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"The nation's president hosted a welcoming ceremony and a banquet ___ honor his visiting Brazilian counterpart.","answer":"in ... of","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Do you believe that Hillary Clinton didn't make it in the American presidential election because as a woman candidate she is discriminated ___?","answer":"against","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["dazzle","figure out","set ... apart","carry off","have the last laugh","cram ... into","have ... in common with","scale up","brush with the law","stand accused of","have a lock on","reinforce","impose","in combination with","be incompatible with","has more in common with","are incompatible with","sets him apart","carried off","has the last laugh","reinforced","brushing with the law","dazzled"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"No one could ___ how he got penniless just as nobody could understand how he got to be so wealthy all of a sudden at the very beginning.","answer":"figure out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Most of us accept unquestioningly that philosophy, an arts subject, ___ history, another arts subject, than it has with physics, a science subject.","answer":"has more in common with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"The living habits of the older generation ___ those of the younger generation, so it's wise for them to live under separate roofs.","answer":"are incompatible with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"They ___ two sins: first, they intrude unreasonably into people's private lives; second, they are unacceptably biased and pursue that bias with scant regard for the truth.","answer":"stand accused of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"His keen and informed interest in the arts, not only ballet but plays, books, music, painting, ___ from most of the other students of science.","answer":"sets him apart","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"There were years when former Soviet Union and Romanian athletes ___ all the prizes in the international gymnastic competition.","answer":"carried off","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Another useful way to use punishment is ___ positive reinforcement.","answer":"in combination with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Nobody thought him promising when Donald Trump declared to run for American president, but he ___ .","answer":"has the last laugh","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The CEO of the company says if it goes as well as expected, decisions will have to be made this year on how best to ___ the operation and where to site the next expansion.","answer":"scale up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"With the deteriorating air quality, the authority has to ___ severe penalty on those enterprises which do great harm to our environment with pollution.","answer":"impose","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"In Pride and Prejudice, the tale Wickham told about Darcy ___ the heroine Elizabeth's dislike of Darcy.","answer":"reinforced","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"If you try to ___ too much ___ one day, your body and mind will fight it with procrastination.","answer":"cram ... into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Does the greater risk of ___ bring with it greater fear of the consequences?","answer":"brushing with the law","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Though the recession hurt the sales of blades and boosted the sales of cheaper disposable razors, the two leading companies still ___ the US market.","answer":"have a lock on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Los Angeles has ___ the world as supreme creator of the Hollywood legend, immortalizing glamor and feeding the minds of 20th and 21st century filmgoers.","answer":"dazzled","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 5 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"中国一线城市的房价近年来增长迅猛。如果政府不采取措施控制疯狂上涨的房价，就会因缺乏调控市场的能力而受到指责。（shoot up, tame, stand accused of）","answer":"The housing prices in the first-tier Chinese cities have shot up in recent years. If the government doesn't make a point of taming the raging/relentlessly rising housing prices, it will stand accused of lacking capabilities to regulate market.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"这两个宗教派别的敌对可以追溯到前殖民时期的17世纪。由于双方的冲突升级为全面战争，刚上任几个月的国家新政府着手解除双方的武装，缓解双方由来已久的敌意。（trace back to, assume, set about, mitigate）","answer":"The hostility of these two religious sects can be traced back to the pre-colonial 17th century. Now that the clash between them escalates into a full-scale war, the nation's new government, which has just assumed its role for a couple of months, sets about disarming their forces and mitigating their longstanding hostility.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"有两个因素可以帮助我们理解为什么这家公司近年来在所有竞争对手中黯然失色：一个因素是产品不断创新，另一个是公司管理层一直致力于提高服务质量。难怪公司销售业绩和股票价格都一路飙升。（throw light on, eclipse）","answer":"Two factors can throw light on why this company has eclipsed all its competitors in recent years. One is constant product innovation and the other is that the company management has been committed to improving customer service. No wonder both its sales and stock prices have shot up.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"当今财阀的影响力不仅仅局限在经济领域，无法遏制权力欲望的财阀们通常会染指政治，与前景看好的政客结成互利互惠的关系。（be confined to, rein in, take a hand in）","answer":"The influence of the plutocrats nowadays is not confined to economic section. Unable to rein in their greedy desire for power, they, more often than not, take a hand in politics, fostering a kind of mutually beneficial relationship with the promising politicians.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"富士康与苹果等许多世界五百强公司对接，致力于为它们的电子产品提供电子元件，这是公司的核心业务。（link up with, constitute）","answer":"Linking up with many top-500 enterprises such as Apple Inc., Foxconn is committed to supplying electronic parts for their electronic gadgets, which constitutes its core business.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 5 英译汉（豪华游艇）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Of all the unnecessary purchases, yachts are among the hardest to justify. Owners of a yacht — generally defined as a vessel longer than 85 feet registered for private use — rarely use their boats more than a month or two a year. Upkeep can cost millions of dollars a year, and yachts typically fall in value after three or four years. A new paint job alone can cost more than $100,000. What's more, international maritime law generally prohibits yacht owners from carrying more than 12 guests, excluding crew members, although some big boats can get permission for 36 guests. That means a yacht can't host large parties while cruising offshore. It's true that large yachts are meant to enhance the reputation of their owners with ultra-rich peers, but when things go wrong, they undermine their image. While nothing stops magnates spending honestly earned billions with as little taste and as much extravagance as they can afford, most superyacht purchases reflect all their worst traits: hubris, personal greed, an over-aggressive need to compete and a disregard for public opinion.","answer":"在所有的非必需品中，游艇属于最没必要的那类。游艇通常指体长85英尺以上的注册私用船舶。拥有游艇的人一年也难得用上一两个月，但维修保养费用一年就得几百万美元。而且游艇一般三四年后就贬值了，光喷漆一项就得花费10万美元。另外根据国际海事法的规定，除船员以外，游艇准载人数通常不超过12人，只有一些大型游艇可以申请准载36人，这就意味着游艇在海上游弋时举行不了盛大派对。拥有游艇确实能替船主在超级富豪同仁中造势，但如果事态发展不妙，游艇也会损毁其形象。尽管什么都不能阻止大亨们竭尽所能以不足观的品味和骄奢无度挥霍掉他们正当赚来的万贯资财，但多数超级游艇的购置反映出的是他们最恶劣的品性：自大、生性贪婪、好胜斗狠、漠视公众意见。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 5 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words given in the box. Some words will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["above","Also","boom","cited","dependent","from","however","reach","standing","set","terms","way","what","who"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"With the population of millionaires soaring to more than two million in the US, the rich are finding it harder to ___ themselves apart.","answer":"set","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Many are turning to supersize luxury consumer products to rise ___ the pack.","answer":"above","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Today's super-wealthy, and the companies that serve them, are creating a whole new category of high-end products that are priced beyond the ___ of mere millionaires.","answer":"reach","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"The luxury ___ stems from a huge increase in personal fortune.","answer":"boom","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"A generally rising stock market, soaring executive compensation, higher real-estate values and lower taxes on the wealthy in 1990s are all ___ as explanation for the rising wealth.","answer":"cited","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"___ , more and more entrepreneurs who started family businesses after World War I are cashing out because of industry consolidation.","answer":"Also","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"The nobles' need for greater wealth made them even more ___ on the king's good graces, and left them less money to spend on arms.","answer":"dependent","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Today, Mr. Wolff says, it's the wealthy themselves ___ are bidding up the price of being on top.","answer":"who","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"For the wealthy to keep their status, they have to compete in ___ of luxury consumption.","answer":"terms","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"The mere fact that this group can pay these prices becomes an indicator of social ___.","answer":"standing","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-wordFill-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Word family 选词填空","modules":["Words"],"instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["manifest (n. manifestation; adj. manifest)","prefer (n. preference; adj. preferential; adv. preferably)","seduce (n. seduction; adj. seductive)","inherit (n. inheritance; adj. inherited)","consult (n. consultant/consultation; adj. consulting)","diverge (n. divergence; adj. divergent)","inherent (n. inherence; adv. inherently)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Lack of confidence in the company itself ___ in a fall in the share price.","answer":"manifested","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Inmates claimed that some prisoners had received ___ treatment.","answer":"preferential","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Originally a political catch phrase of the 19th century, ___ Destiny eventually became a standard historical term, often used as a synonym for the territorial expansion of the United States across North America.","answer":"Manifest","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"They were ___ into buying the washing machine by the offer of a free flight.","answer":"seduced","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Had it not been for an ___ write-off of bad debts, the net loss would have been much lower.","answer":"inherited","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"Our services team helps our clients to solve a wide range of ___ safety, compliance and regulatory challenges.","answer":"consulting","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Russia does not intend to ___ from the United Nations position on this issue.","answer":"diverge","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"I'd like a flat there, ___ in the town centre.","answer":"preferably","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The new prime minister was advised to see an image ___.","answer":"consultant","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Is the human being ___ good or evil? This is one of the classic debates in the history of philosophy and religion.","answer":"inherently","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-idioms-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 6 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The side effects of the treatment have been a cause ___ concern for a while now.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Property tax is the tax liability imposed ___ homeowners for owning real estate.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Do not expand and redirect the ongoing attacks on people of color ___ the name of fighting terrorism.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"I was hoping to stay on for two or three years if my financial situation allows, but it is ___ , I have to leave to look after my family.","answer":"as","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"To be highly effective, software and services have to be proven ___ practice.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"She believed that she had the support of both of them to recruit this deputy, who was to report ___ her.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"It's hard to pinpoint exactly when I went from feeling embarrassed about my difference to taking pride ___ it as it was probably a very gradual transformation.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Bert reached out ___ what he thought was a piece of iron, slung it away when he saw it wasn't.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"Surrounded by people from more than 100 countries who brought their own cultures to the college, I came to consider myself a mosaic ___ many different cultures, with Israeli being the core one.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"These recipes are simply guidelines and don't have to be followed exactly. In fact, I change them up all the time based on what I have ___ hand in my kitchen or yard.","answer":"on","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-complete-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["pave the way for","be bombarded with","cumulative","be overtaken by","take over","justify","morph into","incorporate into","in a ... light","prone to","divergence","wield","refer","plague","take the form of","has taken the form of","incorporate ... into","justified","wielding","morphing into","will pave the way for","references"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The government realizes that corruption now ___ a culture of corruption which encourages high and expensive life style, showing respect for the rich, no fight or negligible fight against corruption and so on.","answer":"has taken the form of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"With the dollar close to its lowest level of the year, the fall in the prices of staples constitutes a ___ from the historical trading pattern.","answer":"divergence","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"If you want to get your work done more efficiently and more cost-effectively, you should ___ technology ___ your business; being tech-savvy is an essential element of managing and marketing your business.","answer":"incorporate ... into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Even if war is fought in the name of all that is holy, righteous and sacred, it is not ___ , for in its core lies the greatest evils man can unleash upon himself.","answer":"justified","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Don't ___ misgivings and fear. Just go full steam ahead!","answer":"be overtaken by","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"The police have come under increased scrutiny for use of excessive force by ramming the gun-___ suspect.","answer":"wielding","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"This situation, although made worse by the war, was a ___ problem dating from the period of colonial dependency.","answer":"cumulative","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"As online sales inevitably outstrip those of bricks-and-mortar stores, this company is threatening to ___ the clothing market.","answer":"take over","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"Some researchers claim women are probably more ___ emotional stress than men \"because of sensitivity to hormone\", so women tend to have higher rates of depression, post-traumatic stress disorder and other anxiety problems.","answer":"prone to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Celebrities are ___ video-game stars, for example, Jean Reno, Ellen Page and Willem Dafoe, whose voices or digital images are used.","answer":"morphing into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"Scientists hope that data from the probe ___ a more detailed exploration of Mars.","answer":"will pave the way for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"If tests come back positive for ___ , park rangers are notified and warning signs are posted to inform the public on how to avoid fleas and protect themselves and their pets from this serious disease.","answer":"plague","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"A study sponsored by the National Football League makes us see game concussions ___ new ___ ; they are caused by blows that are different from what experts traditionally have thought, suggesting that football helmets need better design and testing to prevent the injuries.","answer":"in a ... light","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"In the past, employers typically waited to ask job applicants for ___ until they were serious contenders for a job, though only occasionally at the time of application.","answer":"references","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"At Disney World, you will ___ more Disney souvenirs than ever imagined.","answer":"be bombarded with","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cn-en-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 6 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"勒索病毒在世界蔓延，影响了银行和医院等各类服务系统，这让人们相信网络攻击已经演变成一种危险的安全威胁。（creep, morph）","answer":"The Ransomware Virus was creeping across the world, affecting all kinds of service systems such as banks and hospitals, which led people to believe that cyber attack has morphed into a dangerous security threat.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"关于气候变化的科学共识比以往任何时候都更普遍，即文献中的压倒性证据指出了一个非常明显的事实：全球正在变暖，因为大气中的二氧化碳含量已达到数百万年来前所未有的水平。（overwhelming, pervasive）","answer":"The scientific consensus on climate change is more pervasive than ever, namely the overwhelming evidence in the literature that points to the very clear fact that the globe is warming due to levels of CO2 in the atmosphere that have been unprecedented for several million years.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"这家化妆品电商希望在开业18个月后上市，其网站主要销售各种高端名牌化妆品。（assortment, go public）","answer":"The E-retailer of cosmetics seeks to go public 18 months after its launch, which mainly deals in an assortment of high-end, brand-name cosmetics on its site.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"芬兰大多数女性在接近30岁时组建家庭，首次做母亲的平均年龄徘徊在28岁左右，而美国女性选择更早生育第一胎，平均初育年龄约为25岁。（opt, median）","answer":"Most women in Finland start their families in their late 20s, with the average age of first-time moms hovering around age 28, while in the US women opt to have their first child earlier, with a median first-birth age of about 25.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"他报告说，四十多项针对儿童、青少年和成人整体阅读习惯的国家研究都得出了同样严峻的结论，并呼吁努力重振大众的阅读兴趣。（revitalize, grim）","answer":"He reported that more than forty national studies on the overall reading habits of children, teenagers, and adults had come to the same grim diagnose and called for efforts to revitalize an interest in reading among the general population.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-en-cn-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 6 英译汉（简化英语）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"In 1986 the manufacturers issued their first guide to Simplified Technical English, which was then adopted by the Air Transport Association of America and has since become an international standard. The standard is specific in its instructions, which aim to ensure that once someone has learnt a word in one form, they will not encounter it in another. So manufacturers are told the word \"follow\" should always mean \"come after\" and not \"obey\". So you can say \"obey the safety instructions\" but not \"follow the safety instructions\". You can see why this might be useful in aircraft maintenance books but it would be unnecessarily restrictive in reporting the credit crisis. But at least one news organization has developed a simplified English service, and it did it some time back. The Voice of America broadcast its first program in what it calls \"Special English\" in 1959. This has a slightly bigger vocabulary — 1,500 words. It also has style rules: use short sentences that contain only one idea. Use the active voice. Do not use idioms. And above all, speak slowly. Special English broadcasters speak at two-thirds of normal speed. To a native speaker, the effect is soporific. To a non-native speaker, the increase in comprehension must be thrilling. Simplified English may not be for everyone, but with the rise in the number of people around the world working in English, I suspect we will see more of it.","answer":"悄声细语对君言：说话要慢要简单。1986年，飞机制造商们发布了它们第一部《简化技术英语指南》，随后被美国航空运输协会采用，并自那时起成为一个国际标准。此项标准具体体现在其各项指令当中，这些指令旨在确保一旦人们掌握某个词所表示的意思，就不会遇到该词还表示其他意思的情况。例如，飞机制造商们被告知，单词“Follow”始终应表示“跟随”而不是“遵守”之意。因此，你能够说“Obey（遵守）安全指令”，而不能再说“Follow（遵守）安全指令”。你可以意识到，为什么此项标准在飞机维修书中或许是有价值的，但在报导信贷危机时却会带来不必要的限制。然而，至少有一个新闻机构已开发出简化英语服务，并且距今已有相当一段时间。美国之音于1959年播出了第一期所谓的“特别英语”的节目。该节目的词汇表稍大一些—1500个单词。它还拥有文法规则：使用短句，每句只包含一个意思；使用主动语态；不使用成语；而最为重要的是，语速要慢。“特别英语”节目广播员的语速是正常语速的三分之二。对于一个母语为英语的人来说，它的效果是令人昏昏欲睡。不过对于一个母语非英语的人来说，能增进理解必定是令人兴奋的。简化英语可能不适用于每个人，但是随着全世界工作环境为英语的人数增加，我想我们将看到它的更多应用。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-2-cloze-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 6 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words given in the box. Some words will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["access","certain","channels","combines","convey","interacting","localize","nuances","professionals","specifications"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"While organizations may feel vulnerable knowing that users are ___ in social media worldwide and having constant access to multilanguage news on international portals, marketing and communications professionals wonder what sort of image the corporate brand is going to convey.","answer":"interacting","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"While organizations may feel vulnerable knowing that users are interacting in social media worldwide and having constant ___ to multilanguage news on international portals, marketing and communications professionals wonder what sort of image the corporate brand is going to convey.","answer":"access","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"While organizations may feel vulnerable knowing that users are interacting in social media worldwide and having constant access to multilanguage news on international portals, marketing and communications ___ wonder what sort of image the corporate brand is going to convey.","answer":"professionals","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"marketing and communications professionals wonder what sort of image the corporate brand is going to ___ : What degree of consistency do they need across their communication channels?","answer":"convey","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"What degree of consistency do they need across their communication ___ ?","answer":"channels","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"And to what extent will they have to ___ their procedures and content to fit the linguistic and cultural nuances of the local market?","answer":"localize","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"And to what extent will they have to localize their procedures and content to fit the linguistic and cultural ___ of the local market?","answer":"nuances","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"While there is not an easy answer to all these questions, one thing is ___ : at this stage, the key is to find a balanced method that combines global and local content and meets the requirements of both a global target audience and the locale's linguistic and cultural specifications.","answer":"certain","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"at this stage, the key is to find a balanced method that ___ global and local content and meets the requirements of both a global target audience and the locale's linguistic and cultural specifications.","answer":"combines","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and meets the requirements of both a global target audience and the locale's linguistic and cultural ___.","answer":"specifications","type":"text","module":"Box"}]}]},{"key":"shangying-3","name":"商英教程3","units":[{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["hierarchy (n. hierarchy; adj. hierarchical)","sustain (n. sustainability; v. sustain; adj. sustainable)","cultivate (n. cultivation; v. cultivate)","reverse (n. reversal; v. reverse; adj. irreversible/reversible; adv. irreversibly)","rely (n. reliance; v. rely; adj. reliant)","ignore (n. ignorance; v. ignore; adj. ignorant)","plausible (n. plausibility; adj. plausible; adv. plausibly)","invent (n. invention/inventiveness; v. invent; adj. inventive; adv. inventively)","perceive (n. perception; v. perceive; adj. perceptible; adv. perceptibly)","publicity (n. publicity; v. publicize; adj. public)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"We marvel at man's ___ and skill in putting complex pieces of machinery into space.","answer":"inventiveness","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"He argued very ___ that the claims were true.","answer":"plausibly","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"She showed her great ___ in her assessment of the family situation.","answer":"perception","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"This old tradition is ___ disappearing.","answer":"irreversibly","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Rank in the ___ is related to an individual's income, social prestige, and quality of life.","answer":"hierarchy","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"There has been a lot of advance ___ for her new film.","answer":"publicity","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Irrigation methods should take into consideration of the water sources and the quality of the water.","answer":"sustainability","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"If you sow seeds of satisfaction and pleasure by giving to others and ___ the garden of your soul, there will be flowers in your heart.","answer":"cultivate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"People do not like to ask questions for fear of appearing ___.","answer":"ignorant","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Heavy ___ on one client is risky when you are building up a business.","answer":"reliance","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 1 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"这里的\"可再生资源\"指的是一种理论上可持续利用的地下水资源；不可再生资源只能在紧急情况下使用，而不能持续使用。(sustain)","answer":"The renewable resource here refers to a kind of sustainable groundwater supply in theory, and the non-renewable resource is only for emergency use, not for sustainable use.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"为了在这些项目中处于前沿地位，工程师们不仅需要展示其技术技能，而且要表现出创新性，以及作决断和采取主动的能力。(invent)","answer":"To be at the forefront of such projects, engineers need to display not only technical skills but also inventiveness and the ability to make decisions and take the initiative.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"如果你仍然年轻，那就有可能犯许多错误却没有太多不可挽回的结果。(reverse)","answer":"If you are still young, it is possible to make lots of mistakes without too many irreversible effects.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"人类的感知极其不完善，而且必定是非常主观的。(perceive)","answer":"Human perception is highly imperfect and by definition subjective.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"他辞职了，声称他发现自己成了雪崩式的负面报道的焦点，也无法再有效行使当前的职责。(publicize)","answer":"He resigned, claiming that he had found himself the focus of an avalanche of negative publicity and could not be effective in the current roles.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 1 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Unsatisfied as he was with her proposal, he coupled his refusal ___ much courtesy.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Truly innovative ideas do not arise ___ groups of people, but from individuals.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Apart ___ the balanced diet pyramid, the guides also provide reference for special groups such as babies, pregnant women, aged people and children to have a diet that is good to their health.","answer":"from","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Otherwise more and more of us will all succumb ___ stress-related mental health problems over time.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"An official with the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) said that property income contributed only two percent to the country's per capita disposable income ___.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"The process workshop did not break ___ into such disorder.","answer":"down","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"I simply could not associate a beautiful maiden of the most delicate disposition ___ a name like Black Jade.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"The city ___ one time must have been prosperous, for it enjoyed a high level of civilization.","answer":"at","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"The town is perched ___ the edge of a steep, precipitous cliff.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"China must rely ___ itself to address and resolve problems arising in the process of its peaceful rise.","answer":"on","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 1 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["biodiversity","fundamental","irreversible","rule of thumb","maintain","accumulate","accelerate","involve","ownership","point of view","decline","sparse","surplus","trigger","undermine","irreversibly","undermined"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"But a great book, rich in ideas and beauty, a book that rises and tries to answer great questions, demands the most active reading of which you are capable.","answer":"fundamental","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"If a student's ___ is to study hard, being patient is a teacher's infallible law.","answer":"rule of thumb","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"China Mobile released its acquisition plan of China Railway Communication (China Railcom), which would become the former's wholly-owned subsidiary but ___ independent operation.","answer":"maintain","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Scientists warn that the ecosystem services that support life on Earth, such as capture fisheries and air and water regulation, should be used sustainably lest they ___ destroy the environment.","answer":"irreversibly","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"During the last century, erosion of ___ has been increasingly observed, and some studies show that about one eighth known plant species is threatened with extinction.","answer":"biodiversity","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"The ___ of copyright will depend on whether the journalist was a staff reporter or a freelancer.","answer":"ownership","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"\"Both sides need to discuss Sino-US economic relations from a strategic ___ and map out a better blueprint for future economic and trade relations,\" Wu, head of the Chinese delegation, said.","answer":"point of view","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Construction of the bridge will ___ the flow of goods and talent and give a push to the integration of economic development in the Yangtze River Delta.","answer":"accelerate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The external circumstances of our daily lives are almost wholly dependent upon science and there is scarcely anything in the modern home that has not been made by processes whose principles ___ the scientific advances of recent years.","answer":"involve","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Foods in McDonald's and KFC typically contain high calories and excessive calories will ___ in the form of fat in the body; this may make people overweight.","answer":"accumulate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"Runners carried the Olympic flame around the outside of the Jinnah Stadium in the capital of Islamabad on Wednesday — an invitation-only event in front of a(n) ___ crowd with heavy security.","answer":"sparse","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"He decided to quit his job in that company where efficiency is ___ in a jungle of red tape.","answer":"undermined","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"A fish is also a symbol of ___ in Chinese culture.","answer":"surplus","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Many speculators made money during the ___ of the stock market by fishing in troubled waters.","answer":"decline","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"There are concerns that the raising disparity between booming cities and villages could ___ social discontent.","answer":"trigger","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 1 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"随着地球环境的日益恶化与近年来资源的过度消耗，空气污染、全球变暖等严重的生态危机正威胁着当代人类社会的生存与发展，严重的环境问题使人类社会面临危险。(threaten, endanger)","answer":"With the deterioration of the Earth's environment day by day and the excessive consumption of resources in recent years, such serious eco-crises as air pollution and global warming are threatening the survival and development of contemporary human society, which is being endangered by serious environmental problems.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"我们大家都知道，人类社会正在经历重大变革，而这种变革是由科学及其所派生的技术所引发的。(under way, trigger)","answer":"We are all aware that a dramatic change is under way in human society. The change is triggered by science and the technology it generates.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"当今中国，环境污染和生态破坏已经成为制约我国改革开放进程和经济持续发展的重要因素，大力发展环保产业成为我国保护环境、实施可持续发展战略的重要物质基础和技术保障。(restrain, sustainable)","answer":"In China today, environmental pollution and ecological damage have become important factors that restrain the course of reform and opening-up and the sustainable development of national economy. Developed environment-friendly industries are important material substance and technical guarantee of environmental protection and sustainable development.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"在中国，很多公司在由计划经济向市场经济转轨和商品经济迅速发展的过程中，出现了低效使用或滥用公共资源的现象，从而导致环境污染。(transition)","answer":"In the process of transition from planned economy to market economy and the rapid development of commodity economy in China, the inefficient use or abuse of public resources has been seen in many companies, which has led to environmental pollution.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"冰川大面积融化是人类活动影响全球气候的明显标志，这一观点已获得科学界的公认。(apparent, recognition)","answer":"The opinion has gained wide recognition in the scientific community that the widespread meltdown of glaciers is an apparent sign of the influence of human activities on global climate.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-1","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 1 英译汉（环境警示）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"More wood was removed from forests in 2005 than ever before, one of many troubling environmental signs highlighted on Thursday in the Worldwatch Institute's annual check of the planet's health. The Washington-based think tank's \"Vital Signs 2007-2008\" report points to global patterns ranging from rising meat consumption to Asian economic growth as linked to the broader problem of climate change. The key message of the report was that unsustainable consumption patterns were responsible for climate change linked to carbon emissions and other ecological woes.","answer":"这份报告的主题是，不可持续的消费模式是导致气候变化及与之相关的碳排放和其他生态问题的罪魁祸首。2005年，从森林中砍伐的木材比以往任何一年都要多，这是世界观察研究所周四发布的年度地球健康状况报告中强调的众多令人担忧的环境迹象之一。总部设在华盛顿的这家智库发布的《2007-2008年世界状况》报告指出，从肉类消费增长到亚洲经济增长等全球趋势都与气候变化这个大问题有关。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-1","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 1 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["eroding","collapsing","destructive","overwhelm","shrinking","civilizations","falling","expanding","extinction","rising"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Economic theory and economic indicators do not explain how the economy is disrupting and destroying the earth's natural systems. Nor does it explain why we are in the early stages of the greatest ___ of plants and animals since the dinosaurs disappeared 65 million years ago.","answer":"extinction","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Evidence that the economy is in conflict with the earth's natural systems can be seen in the daily news reports of ___ fisheries,","answer":"collapsing","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"___ forests,","answer":"shrinking","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"___ soils,","answer":"eroding","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"deteriorating rangelands, ___ deserts,","answer":"expanding","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"___ carbon dioxide (CO2) levels,","answer":"rising","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"___ water tables,","answer":"falling","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"rising temperatures, more ___ storms,","answer":"destructive","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"At some point, this could ___ the worldwide forces of progress, leading to economic decline.","answer":"overwhelm","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"The challenge for our generation is to reverse these trends before environmental deterioration leads to long-term economic decline, as it did for so many earlier ___.","answer":"civilizations","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["apply (n. application/applicant; v. apply; adj. applicable/applied)","suffice (n. sufficiency; v. suffice; adj. sufficient; adv. sufficiently)","exhilarate (n. exhilaration; v. exhilarate; adj. exhilarating)","manipulate (n. manipulation/manipulator; v. manipulate; adj. manipulative)","ascend (n. ascendancy/ascension; v. ascend)","concede (n. concession; v. concede)","remedy (n. remedy; v. remedy)","neutral (n. neutrality; v. neutralize; adj. neutral)","refine (n. refinement; v. refine; adj. refined)","degrade (n. degradation; v. degrade; adj. degrading)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"I won't go into all the details. ___ it to say that the whole event was a complete disaster.","answer":"Suffice","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Appraisal has traditionally been seen as most ___ to those in management and supervisory positions.","answer":"applicable","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"It was a(n) ___ experience to be with so many knowledgeable and interesting people.","answer":"exhilarating","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"Under stress these people will appear to be superficial, over-eager and ___.","answer":"manipulative","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"Although geographically linked, the two provinces have long fought for political ___.","answer":"ascendancy","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"She made no ___ to his age; she expected him to work as hard as she did.","answer":"concession","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"He promised to act quickly to ___ any problems, but said: \"It is still a capable and particularly accurate weapon.\"","answer":"remedy","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"The economic situation has been improved recently, and the latest figures should ___ the fears of inflation.","answer":"neutralize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"___ sugars are absorbed into the bloodstream very quickly.","answer":"Refined","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"He said at the conference that they wanted to amend the law to protect children from punishment that was harsh, ___ and inappropriate in a decent society.","answer":"degrading","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 2 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"大多数人认为科学是一个中性的工具。在他们看来，科学只不过给我们提供了有关自然界的知识，或者说赋予了我们权力，但是如何运用这些知识和权力则是我们自己的责任。","answer":"Most people view science as a neutral tool. In their opinion, it simply uses knowledge of the natural world to inform us or empower us, but what we do with that knowledge and power remains up to us.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"纳米技术的应用将会彻底改变我们的生产制造方式。与现今众所周知的技术不同，它对环境不构成任何威胁。","answer":"Application of nanotechnology will bring about a total transformation in the way of manufacturing. Unlike technology as we know it today, it poses no threat to the environment.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"目前已经有足够证据表明干细胞研究将会提供一种全新的方法，用来治疗许多严重的疾病。","answer":"Now there is sufficient evidence that stem cell research will provide a completely new approach to treatment of many serious diseases.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"他对经济政策的陈述、操控国际机构以利于国内形势，以及把对手描述为极端分子的能力都是很有效的手段，可能会被总统采纳。","answer":"His presentation of economic policy, his manipulation of international institutions for domestic advantage and his ability to portray rivals as extremists are all effective tactics that might be adopted by the President.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"近年来，巨大规模的城镇移民和国际移民也表明了一些更加令人不安的趋势：贫富差距增大、人口快速增长、环境日益恶化。","answer":"The magnitude of urban and international migration in recent years is also evidence of more disturbing trends: the expanding gap between rich and poor, rapid population growth and increasing environmental degradation.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 2 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"My eyes slowly grew accustomed ___ the dark.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"I am always wary ___ men wearing suits, as I equate this with power and authority.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Everything was going really well until he came along and fouled things ___.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"His genius was confined ___ the decoration of buildings.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The government has poured millions ___ the education system.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Didn't he feel guilty about feeding ___ their lives in his writing?","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"He rewrote the book in light ___ further research.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Companies are increasingly keen to contract ___ peripheral activities like training.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"They were coerced ___ negotiating a settlement.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"The new catalogue will open ___ the market for our products.","answer":"up","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 2 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["at one stroke","integrated","hint","accustomed","harness","inhaling","transformation","opened up","approach","pose","crowded out","transferred","grounds","in effect","superseded"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"They threatened to cancel the whole project ___.","answer":"at one stroke","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"These programs can be ___ with your existing software.","answer":"integrated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"He gave a broad ___ that he was thinking of retiring.","answer":"hint","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"The two brothers were ___ to living together.","answer":"accustomed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"We must ___ the skill and creativity of our workforce.","answer":"harness","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Local residents needed hospital treatment after ___ fumes from the fire.","answer":"inhaling","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"The way in which we work has undergone a complete ___ in the past decade.","answer":"transformation","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"The issue has ___ deep divisions within the party.","answer":"opened up","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The school has decided to adopt a different ___ to discipline.","answer":"approach","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Drunken drivers ___ a serious threat to other road users.","answer":"pose","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"Small local businesses have been ___ by large multinationals.","answer":"crowded out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"He ___ the property to his son.","answer":"transferred","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"The case was dismissed on the ___ that there was not enough evidence.","answer":"grounds","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"By asking for these particular qualifications, you are, ___, excluding most women from applying.","answer":"in effect","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"Hand tools are relics of the past that have now been ___ by the machine.","answer":"superseded","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 2 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"克隆技术在过去几年中已成为人们关注的焦点。有些人反对克隆人类，理由是它可能引发某些道德问题，令人担忧。(ground, open up, ethical)","answer":"Cloning has become the dominating concern in the past few years. Some people oppose human cloning on the grounds that it may open up some troubling ethical questions.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"科技企业必须要有效地获得技术转让，并将这些新技术融入产品开发，否则就有可能日益激烈的竞争中被排挤出局。(transfer, integrate, crowd out)","answer":"Technology-based businesses must be effective in technology transfer and integrating the new technologies into their product development. Otherwise they will be crowded out with increasingly intense competition.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"考虑到科学研究与技术开发之间的复杂关系，以及科学在现代社会中所起的主导作用，科学家应当小心谨慎，以防科学研究给人类和环境造成影响。(in light of, be wary of)","answer":"In light of the complex relationships of scientific research and technology development and the dominant role played by science in modern society, scientists should be wary of the human and environmental consequences of scientific research.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"实际上，纯科学和应用科学之间的分界线近年来已经变得模糊了。比如在生物技术领域，今天还在实验室里的新奇想法，明天就有可能成为市场上热销的技术。(in effect, novel)","answer":"In effect, the lines dividing pure and applied science have become blurred in recent years. For example, in the field of biotechnology, today's novel ideas in laboratories can become tomorrow's favorite technologies of the marketplace.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"当一种技术经历了重大变革阶段并取得了成功的创新，就成为重要的学习经验。由于网络融合是复合型创新取得成功的关键，所以应鼓励组织内的网络联系和跨功能的协作。(transformation, integration)","answer":"When a technology goes through a major transformation phase and yields a successful innovation, it becomes a great learning experience. Organizational networking and cross-functional collaboration should be encouraged because network integration is the key to success for complex innovation.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-2","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 2 英译汉（纯科学与应用科学）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The tremendous advances in pure science during the 20th Century have completely transformed the relationship between science and society. Science has become a dominant element in our lives. It has yielded many benefits and brought enormous improvements to the quality of life, but has also created grave perils. These include pollution of the environment, the squandering of natural resources, and, above all, a threat to the very existence of the human species through the development of weapons of mass destruction. However, many scientists believe that their work has nothing to do with those problems, on the grounds that there is a clear distinction between pure and applied science.","answer":"20世纪纯科学的巨大进步彻底改变了科学与社会之间的关系。科学已经成为我们生活中的主导因素。它带来了许多好处，极大地改善了生活质量，但也造成了严重的危险。这些危险包括环境污染、自然资源的浪费，以及最重要的是，通过大规模杀伤性武器的发展对人类生存本身构成的威胁。然而，许多科学家认为他们的工作与这些问题无关，理由是纯科学与应用科学之间有着明确的区别。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-2","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 2 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["starting","then","since","now","rise","contrast","first","spreading","those","more"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Manufacturing today works by cutting, grinding or deforming large chunks of matter, and (1) ___ fastening together the remaining pieces into products.","answer":"then","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"(2) ___ methods are very crude.","answer":"Those","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Molecular manufacturing, in (3) ___, will make things by building from the bottom up,","answer":"contrast","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"(4) ___ with the smallest possible building blocks: atoms and molecules.","answer":"starting","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"It plans to be more efficient and make better products that are cleaner, stronger, lighter, and (5) ___ precise.","answer":"more","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"(6) ___ the concept of molecular nanotechnology was (7) laid out, scientists have developed more powerful capabilities in chemistry and molecular manipulation.","answer":"Since","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"(6) Since the concept of molecular nanotechnology was (7) ___ laid out, scientists have developed more powerful capabilities in chemistry and molecular manipulation.","answer":"first","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"(8) ___ word of the promise of nanotechnology is (9) rapidly, governments and businesses are investing billions of dollars in nanotechnology research and development,","answer":"Now","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"(8) Now word of the promise of nanotechnology is (9) ___ rapidly, governments and businesses are investing billions of dollars in nanotechnology research and development,","answer":"Spreading","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and public awareness of nanotech is clearly on the (10) ___, too.","answer":"rise","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["open-mindedness (n. open-mindedness; adj. open-minded)","working-class (adj. working-class; n. the working class)","tight-knit (adj. tight-knit)","32-year-old (adj. 32-year-old; n. a 32-year-old)","long-term (adj. long-term)","less-than-rewarding (adj. less-than-rewarding)","part-time (adj./adv. part-time)","around-the-clock (adj. around-the-clock)","low- or minimum-wage (adj. low- or minimum-wage)","in-kind (adj. in-kind)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The local tax authorities clarified that mooncakes given as gifts by employers to staff members are taxable as part of employees' ___ income.","answer":"in-kind","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"The police arranged for the witness to have ___ protection until the suspect was arrested.","answer":"around-the-clock","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Many businesses are cutting back by employing ___ lower-paid workers.","answer":"part-time","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"The new manager is a self-educated man from a(n) ___ background.","answer":"working-class","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"This career woman is also a dedicated ___ mother of two kids.","answer":"32-year-old","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"There is a(n) ___ Jewish community living in this area.","answer":"tight-knit","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Graduates are finding it more and more difficult to find ___ employment and some of them have to take jobs.","answer":"low- or minimum-wage","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Working as an office clerk in a small company proved to be a(n) ___ experience for her, so she decided to leave at the end of the third year.","answer":"less-than-rewarding","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Benjamin expressed his gratitude for the ___ of his parents, who supported him when he decided to choose a less-trodden road.","answer":"open-mindedness","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"The startup entrepreneurs are encouraged to develop ___ strategic partnerships with multinational technology corporations.","answer":"long-term","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 3 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"放开二胎政策可能会使女性在求职中处于不利地位，因为她们将面临更多工作和家庭平衡的问题。(work-life balance)","answer":"The second-child policy is likely to put women at disadvantage in job hunting because they will face more work-life balance problems.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"有些父母仍然相信\"虎妈\"、\"狼爸\"们那些会用到体罚的粗犷教育方法能够帮助他们把孩子变成\"优胜者\"。(tough-parenting)","answer":"Some parents still believe the tough-parenting methods of \"tiger moms\" or \"wolf dads\", which might involve physical punishment, can help turn their children into \"winners\".","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"当国内玩具市场大批涌入越来越多的外国品牌，加入了残酷无情的竞争，海外市场却向广东的玩具制造商打开了大门。(cut-throat)","answer":"While the domestic toy market has been flooded with a growing number of foreign brands and engaged in cut-throat competition, the overseas market has opened its door widely to Guangdong's toy makers.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"两个公司之间长期的业务合作关系立即开始了，采用了一种包罗万象的市场营销方法，包括全面的市场营销计划和品牌、促销、营销伙伴支持方面的服务。(all-encompassing)","answer":"The long-term business partnership between the two companies starts immediately and takes an all-encompassing marketing approach, which involves comprehensive marketing initiatives and services in branding, merchandising and marketing partner support.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"作为全球信息与通信技术(ICT)行业的领头羊，华为用开明的态度迎接全球化的到来，与国际伙伴密切合作，促进ICT行业和数字经济的发展。(open-mindedness)","answer":"As a global ICT leader, Huawei embraces globalization with open-mindedness and works closely with its global partners to promote the ICT industry as well as the digital economy.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 3 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The growing aversion ___ slaving away in the kitchen has caused more than one in three Americans to eat out every day.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"China will ramp ___ efforts to nurture a fairer environment for market competition and will bolster intellectual property rights protection to attract more foreign investment.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"They trotted ___ the same old excuses for the lack of jobs in the area.","answer":"out","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"They suspected that the former sales manager had traded secret information ___ money.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The school prides itself ___ fostering a spirit of innovation.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Immigrants have contributed ___ British culture in many ways.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Fostering is a full-time job and you should carefully consider how it will fit ___ your career.","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"Many divorced fathers only have access ___ their children at weekends.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"She was elected to serve ___ secretary of the local party.","answer":"as","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"This year, the city's financial budget will allocate 300 million yuan to buoy ___ technical innovation and industrial transformation and upgrading.","answer":"up","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 3 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["unfathomably","triumphant","emulate","envision","overqualified","back on track","on a roll","cross one's mind","in the throes of","pay lip service","in turn","ingenuity","transformation","viability","dynamics","crossed my mind"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"I made a name for myself and I was ___: I couldn't see anything going wrong.","answer":"on a roll","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The relevant authorities just ___ to environmental issues.","answer":"pay lip service","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Our attention to details and commitment to quality ensures that we supply our customers with clothes that can be relied upon — so that you will come to rely upon us ___.","answer":"in turn","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"They hope to ___ the success of other software companies.","answer":"emulate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"As with all other obsessions, it will require creative ___ to come up with something that is reasonable, makes sense and motivates the child.","answer":"ingenuity","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"She tried to get her life ___ after her ten-year marriage ended in divorce.","answer":"back on track","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"After a few unsuccessful attempts, Jack Ma made a(n) ___ return to the world's largest high-tech trade fair with a cutting-edge facial recognition payment system developed by his company.","answer":"triumphant","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Many working-age immigrants are ___ for their positions in the new country.","answer":"overqualified","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"It never ___ that I might lose in the contest.","answer":"crossed my mind","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"This week, the agency will announce the results of a financial ___ assessment of the factory.","answer":"viability","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"The potential damage to international security and world economy would be ___ dangerous.","answer":"unfathomably","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"The way in which we work has undergone a complete ___ in the past decade.","answer":"transformation","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"I watch other people ___ addiction and I don't know how to help.","answer":"in the throes of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Now that China is pushing for a change in the system of global governance through the \"Belt and Road\" initiative, the Chinese and British governments ___ a future \"golden era\".","answer":"envision","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"This question should prompt students to think about the social ___ of their own high schools, taking into account racial, ethnic, religious and economic factors as well as the political and historical contexts in which the students grew up.","answer":"dynamics","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 3 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"根据中国一家重要的全国性报纸最近的一项调查，近一半的读者表示，随着国家高速工业化带来更大的社会压力，他们感到比五年前更加紧张了。(profess)","answer":"According to a recent survey by a leading Chinese national newspaper, nearly half of the readers profess to feel more stressed than five years ago as the country's fast-paced industrialization brings greater social pressures.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"住房价格近年来持续增长。年轻人无法展望未来能挣到足够的钱来支付房款的订金，尽管他们常常一天工作10到14个小时。(envision)","answer":"Housing prices have kept rising in recent years. Young people cannot envision earning enough money to pay a deposit on a home, despite often working 10 to 14 hours a day.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"这些基金将用于扩展中国农村地区的金融服务，增加对新兴经济体金融服务的投资，加强技术和风险控制，促进绿色金融。(ramp up)","answer":"The funds will be used to expand financial services in rural China, ramp up investment in financial services in the emerging economies, strengthen tech and risk control, and promote green finance.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"这个备忘录将提供一个新平台，促进两个公司在业务项目、技术共享和知识创新机会等发展领域的合作，并有助于加强双边经济和贸易合作。(contribute to)","answer":"The memorandum will provide a new platform to promote the co-operation between the two companies in the development of business projects, technology sharing and knowledge creation opportunities. It will also contribute to the enhancement of bilateral economic and trade co-operation between the two countries.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"鉴于国际石油价格可能会进一步下跌，中国应谨慎考虑自身的具体情况。国家发改委星期三公布的新的上限和下限定价机制是一项符合中国当前国情的合理策略。(fit into)","answer":"Given that international oil prices may fall further, China should carefully consider its specific conditions. The new cap and floor pricing mechanism introduced by the National Development and Reform Commission on Wednesday is a sensible strategy that fits into China's current situation.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-3","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 3 英译汉（工作与生活的平衡）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Many Americans are experiencing burnout due to overwork and increased stress. This condition is seen in nearly all occupations from blue collar workers to upper management. Over the past decade, a rise in workplace violence, an increase in levels of absenteeism as well as rising claims for compensation are all evidence of an unhealthy work-life balance. Employee assistance professionals say there are many causes for this situation, ranging from personal ambition and the pressure of family obligations to the accelerating pace of technology. According to a recent study, 1.7 million people consider their jobs and their work hours excessive because of globalization.","answer":"许多美国人正因过度工作和日益增加的压力而经历职业倦怠。从蓝领工人到高层管理人员，几乎所有职业都能看到这种情况。在过去十年中，职场暴力事件的增多、缺勤率的上升以及工伤索赔的增加，都是工作与生活失衡的证据。员工援助专业人士表示，造成这种情况的原因很多，从个人抱负、家庭责任的压力到技术进步的加速。根据最近一项研究，170万人认为全球化的原因导致他们工作过度、工作时间过长。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-3","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 3 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["however","revealing","for","by","means","preserving","than","into","of","to"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It is true that Hispanic organizations now constitute part (1) ___ the multiculturalist coalition and have been very vocal in pushing (2) bilingual/bicultural education.","answer":"of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"(1) It is true that Hispanic organizations now constitute part of the multiculturalist coalition and have been very vocal in pushing (2) ___ bilingual/bicultural education.","answer":"for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"There is increasing evidence, (3) ___, that rank-and-file immigrants are much more traditionally assimilationist (4) than some of their more vocal leaders.","answer":"however","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"(3) There is increasing evidence, however, that rank-and-file immigrants are much more traditionally assimilationist (4) ___ some of their more vocal leaders.","answer":"than","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"For example, most Chinese and Russian immigrant parents in New York City deliberately avoid sending their children to the bilingual-education classes offered (5) ___ them by the public-school system,","answer":"to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"believing that a cold plunge (6) ___ English will be a much more effective (7) means of learning to function in American society.","answer":"into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"(6) believing that a cold plunge into English will be a much more effective (7) ___ of learning to function in American society.","answer":"means","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Hispanics generally show more support for bilingual education, but even here a(n) (8) ___ recent study indicates that an overwhelming number of Hispanic parents see bilingualism primarily as a means of learning English,","answer":"revealing","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"and not of (9) ___ Hispanic culture.","answer":"preserving","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"(10) ___ contrast, multiculturalism is more strongly supported by many other groups — blacks, feminists, gays, native Americans, etc. — whose ancestors have been in the country from the start.","answer":"By","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["panic (n. panic; v. panic; adj. panicky)","hallucinate (n. hallucination; v. hallucinate; adj. hallucinatory)","venerate (n. veneration; v. venerate; adj. venerable; adv. venerably)","miracle (n. miracle; adj. miraculous; adv. miraculously)","capital (n. capital/capitalism/capitalist; v. capitalize; adj. capitalist/capitalistic)","retrospect (n. retrospect; adj. retrospective; adv. retrospectively)","assiduous (n. assiduity; adj. assiduous; adv. assiduously)","exponent (n. exponent; adj. exponential; adv. exponentially)","vicious (n. viciousness; adj. vicious; adv. viciously)","disorient (n. disorientation; v. disorient; adj. disoriented)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The mere fact that Sam is alive is a(n) ___: the doctors who diagnosed him as suffering from lung cancer seven years ago gave him one year to live.","answer":"miracle","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Many American people ___ General Eisenhower during World War II.","answer":"venerated","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"All the guests ___ and screamed when the bomb exploded.","answer":"panicked","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"The peasants' revolt against America's ___ values seems to have fizzled out almost before it started.","answer":"capitalist","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"The police were shocked by the intensity and ___ of these assaults.","answer":"viciousness","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"She was so stunned by this scene that she experienced a moment of total ___.","answer":"disorientation","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Frankly, I was amazed when she took to you so quickly but, in ___, perhaps it's not so surprising after all.","answer":"retrospect","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"A dream is a(n) ___ experience involving a sequence of images, sounds, ideas, emotions, or other sensations usually during sleep.","answer":"hallucinatory","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"He worked ___ to earn the money for his son's education.","answer":"assiduously","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"The policy tried to check the ___ growth of public expenditure.","answer":"exponential","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 4 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"迈克自从决定与一位日本姑娘结婚并在日本定居，就一直在刻苦地学日语。(assiduous)","answer":"Mike has been assiduous in learning Japanese since he decided to settle down in Japan after he married a Japanese girl.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"报纸对他进行了恶毒的攻击，迫使他辞职。(vicious)","answer":"The newspapers launched a vicious attack on him, forcing him to resign.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"在此阶段进行周密的计划将有助于避免最后一刻的恐慌。(panic)","answer":"Careful planning at this stage will help to avoid a last-minute panic.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"这个谷仓被神奇地改造成了一家豪华酒店。(miraculously)","answer":"The barn has been miraculously transformed into a luxury hotel.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"一种怀旧的气氛弥漫在整场演出中。(retrospective)","answer":"A retrospective atmosphere pervaded the whole performance.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 4 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The film testifies ___ the courage of ordinary people during the war.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"One of the report's recommendations is for the creation of a new body to keep regulation ___ check over the long term.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"I must be going home; it's way ___ my bedtime.","answer":"past","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"After all the delays, we were anxious to make up ___ lost time.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"We have managed to get ___ some very tough times.","answer":"through","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"This is to help her to come to terms ___ her early upbringing and make sense of past experiences.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"It's not always possible to keep tabs ___ everyone's movements.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"It has made a remarkable profit, and is expected to notch ___ a million customers next year.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"Pensions will be increased in line ___ inflation.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Organizing the school trip will be a lot of work, so I need some volunteers to help ___.","answer":"out","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 4 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["better off","by necessity","paradox","toil","hierarchy","overwhelm","bound","paralyze","downsize","lean on","wear on","in agony","cancel out","go out (of) the window","get to","gets to","went out (of) the window","leaning on","wore on","overwhelmed","downsized","cancelled out","paralyzed"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"He was lying on the floor ___.","answer":"in agony","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"I am under a lot of pressure at work, and sometimes it ___ me a bit.","answer":"gets to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"As soon as the naughty boys arrived, order ___ .","answer":"went out (of) the window","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Don't lie to her. She's ___ to find out about it.","answer":"bound","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"It is a(n) ___ that in such a rich country there can be so much poverty.","answer":"paradox","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"He was ___ a tree with his eyes closed.","answer":"leaning on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"I was feeling more and more nervous as the evening ___ .","answer":"wore on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"She worked her way up through the corporate ___ to become president.","answer":"hierarchy","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"Many of the jobs are, ___, temporary.","answer":"by necessity","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Harriet was ___ by a feeling of homesickness.","answer":"overwhelmed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"From now on Adam's work is to be sweat and ___.","answer":"toil","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"The country would be ___ if more women were serving in Congress.","answer":"better off","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"The airline has ___ its workforce by 30%.","answer":"downsized","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"The losses in our overseas division have ___ the profits made in the home market.","answer":"cancelled out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The strike action ___ the region's public transport system.","answer":"paralyzed","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 4 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"富裕的人很多都是有特权的精英，他们焦虑的是成就感而不是饥饿。金钱也许无法买到快乐，但是富裕国家的人一般比贫穷国家的人快乐。不过，全世界不管是富人还是穷人都认为感觉愉快和为别人花钱之间有联系，而对大多数人来说，稀缺性提升了很多事情的快乐感。(elite, anxious, pleasure)","answer":"Many rich people are privileged elites who are anxious about fulfillment, not hunger. Money may not buy happiness, but people in wealthier countries are generally happier than those in poor ones. Yet the link between feeling good and spending money on others can be seen among rich and poor people around the world, and scarcity enhances the pleasure of most things for most people.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"无论你怎样小心地计划和准备，不可思议的事情总会发生。你必须设法尽快走出失业的沮丧，及时寻求职业指导。你可以将此变为于己有利的形势，对自己的生活作一些十分必要的改变。(weird, to one's advantage)","answer":"No matter how carefully you plan and prepare, weird things happen. You must manage to get over the job-loss blues as soon as possible, and seek professional guidance in time. You can turn this experience to your advantage, and make some much-needed changes in your life.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"大难不死可以使你更加坚强。创伤带来的压力绝不是唯一的结果。(post-traumatic)","answer":"What doesn't kill you can actually make you stronger. Post-traumatic stress is far from the only possible outcome.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"我们总是想从成功人士那里学习人生真谛，但结果却是一些遭受痛苦折磨的人可能对什么是美好生活最有发言权。(harrowing, ordeal)","answer":"We always want to learn the true essence of life from successful people, but it turns out that some of the people who have suffered harrowing ordeals may have the most to tell us about \"the good life\".","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"要想找到通过逆境成长的更常见的例子，看看生活中最大的挑战之一就行了：为人父母。事实证明生孩子确实降低了幸福水准，但从长远来看，养育孩子是所有人类事业中最值得做、最有意义的工作之一。(adversity, rewarding)","answer":"For a more common example of growth through adversity, look to one of life's biggest challenges: parenting. Having a baby has been shown to decrease levels of happiness. However, over the long haul, raising a child is one of the most rewarding and meaningful of all human undertakings.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-4","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 4 英译汉（收入与幸福）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Did you ever get a job offer, promotion or pay increase that brought you up another level in status and made you feel really good about yourself? But what happened a year later? You felt pretty much the same way you did before the big jump in pay. Your income was up but so were your expenses. You're really not that much happier since you started making more. As people increase their income, they also increase their expectations and what they want out of life. We humans have a tendency to revert to a normative level of happiness even after undergoing major positive or negative life changes.","answer":"你是否曾经得到过一份工作、一次晋升或加薪，使你的地位提升了一个档次，让你自我感觉非常好？但一年后发生了什么？你的感觉跟你收入大幅增加之前几乎一样。你的收入增加了，但你的开销也增加了。自从你开始挣更多的钱，你其实并没有更加快乐：当人们增加了收入，他们也提升了期待值，对生活有了更多的追求。我们人类有一种将幸福恢复到标准水平的倾向，即使经历了重大的人生变故，无论好坏，都能恢复。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-4","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 4 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["at","context","instead","take","through","healthy","under","from","panic","overwhelmed"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"A lot has been mentioned in today's political arena about emotional intelligence and being able to stay calm (1) ___ pressure.","answer":"under","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"It's not that we can control all stress in our lives. Some amount of stress or conflict is actually (2) ___ and keeps us energized.","answer":"healthy","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"We just want to make sure that we can handle the pressures that life throws (3) ___ us.","answer":"at","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"You need to have good self-awareness. Try reframing what is happening and put the issue in (4) ___.","answer":"context","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Get some exercise to divert your mind away (5) ___ your feelings.","answer":"from","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"You need to have a healthy sense of humor about life and not (6) ___ yourself too seriously.","answer":"take","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Being able to laugh at yourself for making a mistake can ease the stress or (7) ___ you feel.","answer":"panic","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Instead of constantly telling others you are (8) ___ or swamped (which might be true), use more positive messaging to say that you will get (9) this.","answer":"overwhelmed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"(8) Instead of constantly telling others you are overwhelmed or swamped (which might be true), use more positive messaging to say that you will get (9) ___ this.","answer":"through","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Using more positive terms instead of negative ones helps you to focus on the light at the end of the tunnel (10) ___ of the tunnel itself.","answer":"instead","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["minimum / minimized","impartial / partiality","popularize / popularity","flexibility / inflexible","informative / informed","established / establishments","exclude / exclusively","disproportionally / proportional","equipped / equipment","obsessive / obsess"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"1. minimum — A. Many of Britain's beaches fail to meet the ___ standards of cleanliness.","answer":"minimum","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"1. minimum — B. Many of these problems can be ___ by sensible planning.","answer":"minimized","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"2. partial — A. An Asian security expert pointed out that she saw the United States making an \"unfortunate departure\" from the ___ position in its Aug 3 statement on the South China Sea issue.","answer":"impartial","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"2. partial — B. We think that the court consisting of arbitrators from both sides must be fair and able to handle the dispute without bias or ___.","answer":"partiality","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"3. popular — A. China plans to ___ consumer finance companies across the country that offers small loans with no collateral to encourage more spending, especially from lower-income groups, amid sluggish demand.","answer":"popularize","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"3. popular — B. With the ___ of Harry Potter novels, the number of children applying to boarding schools has risen.","answer":"popularity","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"4. flexible — A. This report explores the relationship between pay status, work ___ and outcomes such as work-family conflict and work stress.","answer":"flexibility","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"4. flexible — B. This system proves to be really ___ in a fast-changing and increasingly mobile society, so a reform is badly needed.","answer":"inflexible","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"5. inform — A. Rusty's market analysis reached conclusions that are both ___ and instructive for anyone in need of a greater understanding of the North American energy market.","answer":"informative","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"5. inform — B. The providers must tell you about the possible benefits and harms that a reasonable person in your situation would want to know to make an ___ decision.","answer":"informed","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"11","q":"6. establish — A. Even when they understand lessons from the best available research, it can be hard to change ___ beliefs and routines.","answer":"established","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"12","q":"6. establish — B. Tourism benefits not only airlines, hotels, restaurants, and taxi drivers, among others, but also many commercial ___ and even the manufacturers of tourist commodities.","answer":"establishments","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"13","q":"7. exclude — A. Health plans that ___ services used only by women constitute a form of discrimination.","answer":"exclude","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"14","q":"7. exclude — B. Though made in China, and for Chinese ___, the All New C-Class also represented Mercedes' global standard.","answer":"exclusively","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"15","q":"8. proportion — A. Whites continue to be ___ represented in the voting booth: 47% of whites are regular voters, compared with 29% of non-whites.","answer":"disproportionally","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"16","q":"8. proportion — B. Green Party leader Elizabeth May said bringing in ___ representation would likely increase the Green Party's share of the popular vote.","answer":"proportional","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"17","q":"9. equip — A. With a host of technologies borrowed from higher models now ___ as standard, we look forward to exceeding consumer expectations, setting new standards in the segment and truly changing the game.","answer":"equipped","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"18","q":"9. equip — B. An X-rays technician is refusing to do her job until the firm agrees to replace its out-dated ___.","answer":"equipment","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"19","q":"10. obsess — A. She is making an effort to change her ___ tendency that seeks to keep everything in place.","answer":"obsessive","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"20","q":"10. obsess — B. His fans, those who blog about him and follow his tweets, also ___ about those jeans he wears in the pages of Us Weekly.","answer":"obsess","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 5 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"他简化生活，将自己的需求降到最低限度。(minimum)","answer":"He reduced his needs to the minimum by simplifying his life.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"他设法与两个团体都达成了部分协议。(partial)","answer":"He managed to reach a partial agreement with both republics.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"灵活地运用标准比死守标准显得更合情合理。(flexible)","answer":"It would seem more sensible to apply standards flexibly rather than rigidly.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"如今奢侈品包含了排他性，甚至几乎是唯一性，并非因为它是给少数人的。(exclude)","answer":"Today luxury involves exclusiveness, nearly uniqueness, not because it is addressed to few people.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"人类一直痴迷于试图捕捉时间的意义。(obsess)","answer":"Humanity has been obsessed with trying to capture the meaning of time.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 5 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The valuable collections of art are enshrined ___ handsome buildings, mostly in the suburbs on the north side of the town.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"The mobile phone provides a link that we often take ___ granted to the people to whom we are closest; when we are without it, social and domestic disarray may result.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"Scientists announced another breakthrough in their quest ___ a cure for prostate cancer.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"Vitamins and minerals are essential to any diet, and research suggests they may help prevent cancer and heart disease, not ___ mention other health problems.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"The bill for health services can quickly add up if a lot is needed over time, and there is no annual limit on how much you might need to pay ___ pocket.","answer":"out of","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Once the foremost power in South America, Brazil now seems to be ___ the brink of collapse and the investor confidence is undermined by deepening political turmoil and public dissatisfaction.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"He persuaded the companies with a long history and people that have means to make it a priority ___ invest in businesses of these disadvantaged communities.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"The tall rectangular buildings may well give way ___ a more complex and exciting shape.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"It is easier to get ___ debt than to get out of it again!","answer":"into","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Although Brook said that the company had already cut back ___ contracts with external recruitment services, the changes did not go far enough.","answer":"on","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 5 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["confined to","halt","betrayal","Granted","at the disposal of","entitle","trigger","exclusive","affiliate","not to mention","get out","cater to","cling to","status quo","on a trial basis","entitles","affiliated","gets out","caters to","clung to"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Some animals in factory farms spend their lives ___ concrete stalls and metal cages, terrified and suffering in such unnatural conditions.","answer":"confined to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"The IRA leadership has called a(n) ___ to its campaign of violence.","answer":"halt","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"His statement was a(n) ___ of his ignorance on the subject.","answer":"betrayal","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"___ that Tom has enough money to buy the car, it doesn't mean he's going to do so.","answer":"Granted","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The nice-looking young man with soft features and polished manners evidently considered himself a celebrity but out of politeness modestly placed himself ___ the circle in which he found himself.","answer":"at the disposal of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"This coupon ___ you to a 10 percent discount.","answer":"entitles","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"We were afraid that the sparks from the engine would ___ an explosion.","answer":"trigger","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"The reporter managed to get a(n) ___ interview with the Prime Minister.","answer":"exclusive","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"In some instances colleges are supported entirely by one county; in others a college is ___ by several counties.","answer":"affiliated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"I enjoyed the meal in such a cozy restaurant, ___ the conversation with the novelist.","answer":"not to mention","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"You should be fully aware that if the secret ___ , there will be trouble.","answer":"gets out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"It is the kind of movie that ___ the worst side of human nature.","answer":"caters to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"The mother ___ the hope that she might see her son again one day.","answer":"clung to","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Taking your friend for granted is typically associated with stability and confidence in the ___, which can lead to the assumption that no further effort or resources need to be invested.","answer":"status quo","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The bicycle club planned to organize four rides for this summer ___; two in July and two more in August.","answer":"on a trial basis","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 5 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"加拿大商会的首席执行官哀叹道：\"高技术人员流动性极大，这对雇主和政府投钱给培训项目起到了抑制作用，他们担心新近培训的工人都被挖走。\"(lament, disincentive)","answer":"The CEO of the Canadian Chamber of Commerce lamented, \"Highly skilled people are extremely mobile, which creates disincentives for employers and government to pour money into training programs, lest all those newly skilled workers get poached.\"","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"最好的销售方法必须能跟上产品、消费者和技术的改变。成功地运用这些方法会引发一连串积极的结果，进而产生更好的成绩。(keep pace with, beget)","answer":"The best sales practices have to evolve to keep pace with the changes in products, customers and technology. Success in applying the practices will beget a chain of positive results to in turn generate even better performance.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"支持者宣称失业部分是由复杂和不容变更的劳动法所致，他们认为这些法律还阻碍了企业的设立和扩张，使经济增长维持在低水平。(inflexible, partial)","answer":"Supporters claim that unemployment is partially caused by the complex and inflexible labor laws which they believe have also helped keep economic growth at a low level by discouraging business foundation and expansion.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"回忆起所经历的事时，他很愤怒：我们所有的电器、家具都被大火吞噬了。这可是一辈子的投入，十分钟就化为灰烬了。(exasperated, investment)","answer":"He was exasperated when he recalled what he had experienced: Every electronics and appliances and furniture that we have were devoured by fire. That is a lifetime of investment and it was ashes in ten minutes.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"针对被高失业率和经济下滑所困扰的\"衰退\"中的城市，政府将拨款解决问题，用于当地的社会保障、医疗、教育和环境恢复项目。但是，在资源利用效率方面表现不好的地区将得到较少的资金。(deteriorating, fare)","answer":"For the \"declining\" cities plagued by high unemployment levels and deteriorating economy, the government will tackle the problems by allocating funds to be used for local social security, health care, education and environmental restoration projects. However, those who fare poorly in resource utilization efficiency will get less funding.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-5","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 5 英译汉（寿命与退休）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"According to a recent report, life expectancy in the United States is the longest ever, approaching 79 years. This was highlighted in the recent Time cover story, \"This Baby Could Live to Be 142 Years Old.\" With very few exceptions — such as the flu pandemic of 1918, which caused the life expectancy to temporarily plummet by a dozen years — our life expectancy has continued with a positive trend line throughout our nation's history. Now, as life expectancy approaches 79, the full retirement age for Social Security has increased from 65 in 1960 to 67. Hence, on average, it will now be necessary for Social Security benefits to fund 12 years of retirement.","answer":"根据最近的一份报告，美国人的预期寿命达到了有史以来的最高水平，接近79岁。最近《时代》杂志的封面故事《这个婴儿可以活到142岁》着重强调了这一点。除了极少数例外——如1918年的流感大流行曾使预期寿命暂时骤降了十几岁——在我们的国家历史上，预期寿命一直保持着积极的上升趋势。如今，随着预期寿命接近79岁，社会保障的完全退休年龄已从1960年的65岁提高到67岁。因此，平均而言，现在社会保障福利需要为12年的退休生活提供资金。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-5","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 5 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["demand","higher","Japanese","known","margin","more","protectionism","quotas","taking","this"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It is the stated policy of most First World countries to eliminate (1) ___ through free trade policies enforced by international treaties and organizations such as the World Trade Organization.","answer":"protectionism","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Despite (2) ___, many of these countries still place protective and/or revenue tariffs on foreign products to protect some favored or politically influential industries.","answer":"this","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"This creates an artificially profitable industry that discourages foreign innovation from (3) ___ place.","answer":"taking","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Protectionist quotas can cause foreign producers to become (4) ___ profitable, mitigating their desired effect.","answer":"more","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"This happens because quotas artificially restrict supply, so it is unable to meet (5) ___; as a result the foreign producer can command a premium price for its products.","answer":"demand","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"These increased profits are (6) ___ as quota rents.","answer":"known","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"For example, in the United States (1981-1994), Japanese automobile companies were held to voluntary export (7) ___.","answer":"quotas","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"These quotas limited the supply of (8) ___ automobiles desired by consumers in the United States (1.68 million, raised to 1.85 million in 1984, and raised again to 2.30 million in 1985),","answer":"Japanese","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"increasing the profit (9) ___ on each automobile more than enough (14% or about $1,200 in 1983, about $2,300 in 2005) to cover the reduction in the number of automobiles that they sold,","answer":"margin","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"leading to greater overall profits for Japanese automobile manufacturers in the United States export market, and (10) ___ prices for consumers.","answer":"higher","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["audacious (n. audacity; adj. audacious; adv. audaciously)","conceive (n. conception; v. conceive; adj. conceivable; adv. conceivably)","pervade (v. pervade; adj. pervasive; adv. pervasively)","deconstruct (n. deconstruction; v. deconstruct; adj. deconstructive)","appropriate (n. appropriation; v. appropriate)","subvert (n. subversion; v. subvert; adj. subversive)","nostalgia (n. nostalgia; adj. nostalgic; adv. nostalgically)","resonate (n. resonance; v. resonate; adj. resonant)","opulent (n. opulence; adj. opulent; adv. opulently)","disconcert (v. disconcert; adj. disconcerting/disconcerted; adv. disconcertingly)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"It was ___ of him to tell me a downright lie.","answer":"audacious","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"The disease could be ___ transferred to humans.","answer":"conceivably","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"A sense of social change is ___ in her novels.","answer":"pervasive","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"One consequence of ___ is that certainty in textual analyses becomes impossible.","answer":"deconstruction","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"The film company sued them over their ___ of a cartoon character.","answer":"appropriation","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"He was arrested in parliament on charges of ___ for organizing the demonstration.","answer":"subversion","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"People look back on the war period ___, simply because everyone pulled together.","answer":"nostalgically","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"His voice sounded oddly ___ in the empty room.","answer":"resonant","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"Most of the cash went on supporting his ___ lifestyle.","answer":"opulent","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"He was ___ to find his fellow diners already seated.","answer":"disconcerted","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 6 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"我们要提高中低收入居民的收入水平，特别要千方百计增加农民收入，还要适当增加公务员的工资。(conceivably)","answer":"We will increase the income level of the residents with medium and low income. Special efforts will be made to increase farmers' income by every conceivable means. The income of public servants will also be properly increased.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"科学技术已经开始渗透到我们生活的各个领域，其结果是社会正以空前的速度发生着变化。(pervade)","answer":"Science and technology have come to pervade every aspect of our lives and, as a result, society is changing at a speed which is quite unprecedented.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"这本书描述的是两国之间表现在经济、政治和颠覆活动方面的敌对状态。(subversive)","answer":"The book describes a state of hostility between the two countries expressed in economic, political, or subversive action.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"他凶狠地对待朋友，却对陌生人和悦有加，这个习惯令人不快，惹恼了很多人。(disconcerting)","answer":"His disconcerting habit of greeting friends ferociously and strangers charmingly upset a lot of people.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"法律保护商业机密不被非法盗用。(appropriation)","answer":"The law protects trade secrets from wrongful appropriation.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 6 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"He had planned to go skiing on his own in March, but his wife put her foot ___, forcing him to postpone it until April.","answer":"down","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"Turning the company ___ won't be easy.","answer":"around","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"It will take about an hour to get there, allowing ___ traffic delays.","answer":"for","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"I have taken ___ waking up very early.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"Allegations of corruption were leveled ___ him and his family.","answer":"at","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"His firm eventually merged ___ Time Warner.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"People of my generation who lived ___ World War II have vivid memories of confusion and incompetence.","answer":"through","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"His normal style when confronted ___ an obstacle was to bulldoze it into submission.","answer":"with","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"We encourage students to fully participate ___ the running of the college.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"The company closed ___ operations and began liquidating its assets in January.","answer":"down","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 6 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["manipulate","underestimate","degenerate","confine","conceal","at variance with","contractually","imbue with","undermine","viable","capture","impending","fixated on","intoxicating","convergence","capturing","manipulating","undermined","imbued with","concealment","underestimated"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"There is no ___ alternative to solving the current energy crisis except developing solar energy.","answer":"viable","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Driven by a desire for revealing secret human emotions, he started a new novel ___ moments of crisis in common people's life.","answer":"capturing","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Each story reflects a(n) ___ of personal history, cultural assumption and current relationships.","answer":"convergence","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"During 1937 the German museums were systematically purged of \"___ art\".","answer":"degenerate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"He was a past master at ___ the media for his own ends.","answer":"manipulating","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Please ___ your remarks to the subject we are debating.","answer":"confine","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Our confidence in the team has been seriously ___ by their recent defeats.","answer":"undermined","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"When she started speaking, her voice was ___ an unusual seriousness.","answer":"imbued with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"He remembered with mortification how he had forgotten his proud reserve, and his habitual ___ of his feelings.","answer":"concealment","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"These conclusions are totally ___ the evidence — this essay needs to be rewritten.","answer":"at variance with","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"They are obliged to finish the work ___ on time.","answer":"contractually","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"Though the employees expressed their objection, the boss was still ___ automating the office.","answer":"fixated on","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Even without the alcohol, living in New Beginnings can be ___.","answer":"intoxicating","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"While human memory is fragile and subject to change, it should not be ___.","answer":"underestimated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"On the morning of the expedition I woke with a feeling of ___ disaster.","answer":"impending","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 6 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"对艺术的欣赏令人陶醉，因为我们都喜爱美好的事物，也都被这种喜爱所驱使而参与到对美的无尽追寻之中。(intoxicating, driven)","answer":"The appreciation of art can be intoxicating, because we all love beauty and we are all driven by this love to participate in the endless search for beauty.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"经过多年不懈的努力，具有中华民族特色的民间歌曲、舞蹈、戏曲、传说等艺术表现形式，通过赋予新意和更高的表现手段得以改进和创新。这既符合人类历史发展的规律，又顺应了时代潮流。(imbue with)","answer":"After years of unremitting efforts, folk songs, dances, dramas, tales and other forms of artistic expression which are imbued with the characteristics of the Chinese nation have been refined and innovated with new ideas and higher forms of expression. This is not only in accordance with the law of the historical development of mankind, but also in conformity with the trend of the times.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"如果文艺工作者长期脱离生活实际，他们的作品以及他们对于文艺方针问题的意见中，就不免或多或少地发生和大众的需要不相符合的情形。因此，文艺工作者要深入群众、深入生活，为人民奉献更多无愧于时代的作品。(at variance with)","answer":"If writers and artists are divorced from reality for long, their works and their views on the guiding principles for literature and art may inevitably be more or less at variance with the needs of the general public. Therefore, they should go deep among the masses and into the thick of life so as to contribute to the people more works worthy of the times.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"但是从今年前两个月外贸进出口的情况看，要完成今年国家外贸发展的预期目标，仍有较大的困难，对此决不能低估。(underestimate)","answer":"The situation of foreign trade import and export in the first two months, however, indicates there will be fairly great difficulties in fulfilling the foreign trade development plan set for this year, which should not be underestimated.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"人们普遍认为，在工作的时候需要控制个人情感。如果对非工作环境下发生的事情总是念念不忘，就会极大地降低工作效率，这将影响成功的机会。(fixated on, undermine)","answer":"It is generally acknowledged that one needs to hold his personal feelings in check while at work. If one is always fixated on issues happening outside the workplace, his work efficiency will be greatly decreased, which will undermine the chances of success.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-6","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 6 英译汉（艺术与商业）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"The idea of two cultures stuck at either ends of the same bridge can be applied to art and business today. If brand and artist know what they stand for, they should be able to find some common ground. Having the humility to know what you are not cut out for, and the strength to focus on what you do well; to adapt and incorporate outside expertise to enable you to make your dreams reality: these are the ways human achievement has always come about. Art and entrepreneurialism are two expressions of one shared desire: to leave the world a little different than you found it.","answer":"两种文化卡在同一座桥两端的说法，同样适用于当今的艺术与商业。如果品牌和艺术家知道自己代表什么，他们就应该能够找到一些共同点。要有谦逊之心，知道自己不适合做什么；要有力量，专注于自己擅长的事；要懂得适应并吸纳外部的专业知识，使自己的梦想成真：人类成就历来都是这样取得的。艺术和企业家精神是同一个愿望的两种表达：让世界因你而变得有点不同。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-6","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 6 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["more","like","thus","spark","that","simply","fostered","for","ever","as"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"There has been a lot of talk about the need for innovation in business lately. Where does this innovation come from (1) ___ businesses struggle to remain on top and come out with products that corner and change the market place?","answer":"as","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"Is it (2) ___ that business executives try to hire creative people, who are also reliable, and accept the fact that, (3) having blue eyes or green eyes, some people are creative and some aren't?","answer":"simply","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"(2) Is it simply that business executives try to hire creative people, who are also reliable, and accept the fact that, (3) ___ having blue eyes or green eyes, some people are creative and some aren't?","answer":"like","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Or can creativity and innovative thinking be (4) ___?","answer":"fostered","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Today's business environment demands innovation and creativity more than (5) ___.","answer":"ever","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Those who appreciate creativity in these forms are often (6) ___ inspired and open-minded to non-linear approaches to business problem thinking.","answer":"more","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"And having art pieces around them and in the office can (7) ___ those creative inspirations,","answer":"spark","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"(8) ___ aiding the business.","answer":"thus","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"As arts education is slashed left and right in the schools as something not necessary to creating a competent work force, it is interesting to hear that exposure to the arts might make (9) ___ more innovative business leaders,","answer":"for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"and (10) ___ some leading business professionals value exposure to the arts as one of the means for establishing multi-dimensional, and thus, more competitive employees.","answer":"that","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-7","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 7 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["proliferate (v. proliferate; n. proliferation)","picky (adj. picky; adv. pickily)","credit (n. credit; v. credit; adj. credible)","consolidate (v. consolidate; n. consolidation)","adherent (n. adherent/adherence; v. adhere)","predicament (n. predicament)","pricey (adj. pricey; n. price)","teem (v. teem; adj. teeming)","fitful (adj. fitful; adv. fitfully)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"I wonder why you cannot ___ her explanation.","answer":"credit","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Norris twice knocked down his ___ in the early rounds of the fight.","answer":"opponent","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Books and articles on the subject have ___ over the last year.","answer":"proliferated","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"Although ___, Knightsbridge and Sloane Street are among the chicest and most sophisticated shopping areas in London.","answer":"pricey","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"He is a pious ___ of Buddhism.","answer":"adherent","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"They are living in the ___ caused by the failure of two sovereign governments to resolve their difficulties.","answer":"predicament","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"Colin drifted off into a(n) ___ sleep.","answer":"fitful","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"Across the forest, there is a river ___ with fish.","answer":"teeming","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The business needed to invest heavily to meet the demands of car manufacturers who were seeking to ___ their supply chains.","answer":"consolidate","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Some people are very ___ about who they choose to share their lives with.","answer":"picky","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-7","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 7 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"南希有三个挑食的孩子，都喜欢高脂肪的食物。(picky)","answer":"Nancy has three kids who are very picky eaters and prefer food with a high fat content.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"这些早期遗物被认为具有神奇的力量。(credit)","answer":"The relics are credited with miraculous powers.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"这个决定将使她陷入一个独特的困境。(predicament)","answer":"The decision will leave her in a peculiar predicament.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"一年中的大部分时间里，这个地区游人如织。(teeming)","answer":"For most of the year, the area is teeming with tourists.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"为提高效率，这两家公司已合并。(consolidate)","answer":"The two companies have consolidated for greater efficiency.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-7","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 7 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"He had flown to the north of the country to drum ___ support for the campaign.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"In a town with three stoplights, no movie theater and Old Glory waving down at the courthouse, residents take pride ___ tradition.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"He is fed up with people writing him ___ because of his age.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"I have grown up now and I have to face up ___ my responsibilities.","answer":"to","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"He looked relaxed and determined as he fended ___ questions from the press.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"The police kept track ___ the kidnapper using electronic surveillance equipment.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"Paintings are lifeless images rendered in colorful goop. But at night, they take ___ a life of their own.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"We eventually wound ___ staying in a little hotel a few miles from town.","answer":"up","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"Sandra was determined to become a doctor and her persistence paid ___.","answer":"off","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Her career ground ___ a halt when the twins were born.","answer":"to","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-7","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 7 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["accentuate","cutting edge","huff and puff","nuisance","purveyor","sceptic","credential","virtually","tenure","lip service","mercenary","fevered","monitor","nonpartisan","well-placed","huffed and puffed","credentials","sceptics","accentuated","mercenaries","monitoring"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"California is on the ___ of trends that spread nationwide.","answer":"cutting edge","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"They ___ about the price, but eventually they paid up.","answer":"huffed and puffed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Organizations close to the grass roots are ___ to provide certain kinds of information for early warning systems to complement the coarse data provided by satellite.","answer":"well-placed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"In the growing season, weeds were a terrible ___.","answer":"nuisance","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"In the late 1970s, Stuart produced over forty musical, video and theatre performances, which established his ___ as an artist of world-wide renown.","answer":"credentials","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"The government must still convince the ___ that its policy will work.","answer":"sceptics","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"The fundamental patterns of inequality have remained and have been ___ by the war.","answer":"accentuated","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"We all like Mr. Edwards because he is a(n) ___ of joy and laughter.","answer":"purveyor","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The truth was that there were very few ___ he respected, and even fewer he actually liked.","answer":"mercenaries","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"If they are to pay anything more than ___ to this campaign, they should use that power.","answer":"lip service","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"The CIA was ___ his phone calls.","answer":"monitoring","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"That book is clearly the product of a(n) ___ imagination.","answer":"fevered","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"Throughout his long ___, Harry concentrated on administrative matters and avoided publicity for himself and his office.","answer":"tenure","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"Childreach is the U.S. member of PLAN International, the non-profit, ___, non-sectarian organization you may know as Foster Parents Plan.","answer":"nonpartisan","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The legendary library of Alexandria boasted that it had a copy of ___ every known manuscript in the ancient world.","answer":"virtually","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-7","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 7 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"惠普今天宣布了将其设在全世界的85个数据中心合并为位于美国三个城市的六个加大中心的计划。(consolidate)","answer":"HP today announced plans to consolidate its 85 data centers worldwide into six larger centers located in three U.S. cities.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"如果我们不能消除腐败、压制和动荡，利益集团和不良政策就会泛滥，国家就会陷入僵局。(proliferate)","answer":"Interest groups and bad policies would proliferate, and the nation would stagnate, if we cannot get rid of corruption, repression and instability.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"当然，我们也接受这样一个悖论，世界和平似乎以一种奇怪的方式依赖于我们斥巨资购买足以将我们全部消灭的武器。(paradox)","answer":"Of course, we accept the paradox that in some odd way world peace appears to depend on our spending millions of pounds on weapons that would kill us all.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"公众向该公司投诉如潮，力图使涨价被撤销。(endeavor)","answer":"The public bombarded the company with complaints in an endeavor to have the price increases revoked.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"现在人质们获释的主要希望在于国会议员、前安全部长格兰特，他被请来居间调停。(mediate)","answer":"The main hope for the hostages' release now lies with Grant, a congressman and former security minister, who has been invited to mediate.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-7","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 7 英译汉（公共关系）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"If we examine some of the goals and objectives of public relations, it becomes clear that it is a multifaceted activity involving many different functions. Topping the list of objectives, public relations seeks to create, maintain, and protect the organization's reputation, enhance its prestige, and present a favorable image. Studies have shown that consumers often base their purchase decision on a company's reputation, so public relations can have a definite impact on a company's sales and revenue. Public relations can be an effective part of a company's overall marketing strategy. In the case of a for-profit company, public relations and marketing may be coordinated to be sure they are working to achieve the same objectives.","answer":"如果我们研究一下公共关系的某些目标和宗旨，就会发现它是一项涉及许多不同职能的多方面活动。在诸多目标中，公关活动旨在创造、维护和保护组织的声誉，提升其威望，并展现一个良好的形象。研究表明，消费者往往根据公司的声誉来决定是否购买其产品，因此公关对公司的销售额和收入绝对有影响。公关可以是公司整体营销策略的一个有效部分。对于以营利为目的的公司来说，公关和营销可以协调进行，以确保它们朝着相同的目标努力。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-7","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 7 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["at","in","strikes","translate","versa","both","information","public","relations","responsibility"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"To a large extent, the job of public relations is to optimize good news and to forestall bad news, but when disaster (1) ___, the public relations practitioner's task, in consultation with legal counsel, is to assess the situation and the damage,","answer":"strikes","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"to assemble the facts, together with necessary background (2) ___, and to offer these to the news media, along with answers to their questions of fact.","answer":"information","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"When a client is under attack, it is a public relations (3) ___ to organize the client's response — usually involving several complicated issues —","answer":"responsibility","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"to be (4) ___ lucid and persuasive.","answer":"both","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"Government relations are often included (5) ___ public relations under the general designation of public affairs and encompasses lobbying.","answer":"in","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"Industrial relations (i.e., labour-management relations), employee relations, and customer (6) ___ sometimes are accounted part of public relations.","answer":"relations","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"Modern corporate executives often do not excel (7) ___ public speaking or writing in nonbusiness language,","answer":"at","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"and a duty of public relations is to (8) ___ executives' knowledge into speeches or articles intelligible to nonspecialists.","answer":"translate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"In fact, the prime responsibility of public relations can be seen as interpreting the client to the (9) ___ and vice (10) ___.","answer":"public","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"(9) In fact, the prime responsibility of public relations can be seen as interpreting the client to the public and vice (10) ___.","answer":"versa","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-8","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 8 Word family 选词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["profiteer (n. profiteer; v. profiteer; n. profiteering)","mass production (n. mass production; adj. mass-produced)","snobbish (n. snobbery/snob; adj. snobbish; adv. snobbishly)","graft (n. graft; v. graft)","cynicism (n. cynicism; n./adj. cynic/cynical; adv. cynically)","axiom (n. axiom; adj. axiomatic)","perilous (n. peril; adj. perilous; adv. perilously)","excursion (n. excursion)","nimble (adj. nimble; adv. nimbly)","environs (n. environs)","speculative (n. speculation/speculator; v. speculate; adj. speculative; adv. speculatively)","distributor (v. distribute; n. distribution/distributor)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"a person who makes a lot of money in an unfair way","answer":"profiteer","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"the process of producing goods in large quantities, using machinery","answer":"mass production","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"thinking that having a high social class is very important","answer":"snobbish","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"the use of illegal or unfair methods, especially bribery, to gain advantage in business, politics, etc.","answer":"graft","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"the belief that sth good will not happen or that sth is not important","answer":"cynicism","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"a rule or principle that most people believe to be true","answer":"axiom","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"very dangerous","answer":"perilous","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"a short journey made for pleasure, especially one that has been organized for a group of people","answer":"excursion","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"able to think and understand quickly","answer":"nimble","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"the area surrounding a place","answer":"environs","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"11","q":"done in the hope of making a profit but involving the risk of losing money","answer":"speculative","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"12","q":"a person or company that supplies goods to shops/stores, etc.","answer":"distributor","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-wordFill-8-b","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 8 Word family 选词填空（用词填空）","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with the proper forms of the words given.","modules":["Words"],"wordBanks":[{"module":"Words","words":["profiteer (n. profiteer; v. profiteer; n. profiteering)","mass production (n. mass production; adj. mass-produced)","snobbish (n. snobbery/snob; adj. snobbish; adv. snobbishly)","graft (n. graft; v. graft)","cynicism (n. cynicism; n./adj. cynic/cynical; adv. cynically)","axiom (n. axiom; adj. axiomatic)","perilous (n. peril; adj. perilous; adv. perilously)","excursion (n. excursion)","nimble (adj. nimble; adv. nimbly)","environs (n. environs)","speculative (n. speculation/speculator; v. speculate; adj. speculative; adv. speculatively)","distributor (v. distribute; n. distribution/distributor)"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Food safety incidents exposed by the media present rising trend year by year. A large number of \"black workshops\" ___ from selling fake goods, and even some well-known enterprises pursue their own interests at the expense of public interests.","answer":"profiteer","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"2","q":"Included in the tour is a(n) ___ to the Huangguoshu Waterfall.","answer":"excursion","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"3","q":"Institutions such as the unique Académie Française actively sought to prevent a creeping \"Franglais\" brought about by economic and cultural globalization that was perceived, often rather ___, to be nothing more than an Anglo-Saxon invasion.","answer":"snobbishly","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"4","q":"A former senior official was sentenced 12 years for ___ — taking advantage of his official posts to seek benefits for others in construction projects, loans and job reassignments.","answer":"graft","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"5","q":"At its very worst, ___ can generate what Robert Frost articulated in The Death of the Hired Man: the predicament of having \"nothing to look backward to with pride, and nothing to look forward to with hope\".","answer":"cynicism","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"6","q":"The first goal to implement the real estate regulation is to restrain the ___ demand in real estate market and contain rising housing prices.","answer":"speculative","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"7","q":"A food service ___ purchases, stores, sells, and delivers food products, functioning as an intermediary between food manufacturers and food service operators.","answer":"distributor","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"8","q":"He believes in the ___ that the act of forgiveness is not really a gift to others as much as it is a gift to oneself.","answer":"axiom","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"9","q":"The process is characterized by ___ to achieve high volume, elaborate organization of materials flow, careful supervision of quality standards, and minute division of labour, so lower cost does not mean lower quality.","answer":"mass production","type":"text","module":"Words"},{"index":"10","q":"Mary can never forget that ___ journey across the mountains.","answer":"perilous","type":"text","module":"Words"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-wf-8","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 8 汉译英（Word family）","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"自命不凡还可以是享受优质饮品或者出入最高级的美术馆，而不必是穿着浮华、高调的服饰以表达个性。(snobbery)","answer":"Snobbery is also an enjoyment of quality beverages or the classiest art museum around. You don't need to be flashy and loud with your fashion statements.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"国家环保总局说：在京津冀地区及周边的70个城市中，30个受到重度空气污染的影响，另外20个则是中度污染。(environ)","answer":"Among the 70 cities in the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei region and its environs, 30 cities are affected by \"severe\" air pollution, and 20 others are \"heavily\" polluted, the Ministry of Environmental Protection said.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"这本关于投资的书由精明的投资者所著，是成功投资人士的必读宝典。(speculation, speculator)","answer":"This book, written on speculation, by a nimble speculator, is the bible for successful speculators.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"总有一天我们要么陷入最终的麻木，结束这一切，要么醒悟过来，看到我们的危机的真相，这个如生活本身一样宏大的真相。(peril)","answer":"One day we will either sink into the final coma and end it all or awaken to the truth of our peril, a truth as great as life itself.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"这个展览则在探讨工业技术对批量生产的家用产品的影响。(mass-produced)","answer":"This exhibition aims to examine the impact of industrial techniques on mass-produced objects for the home.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-idioms-8","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"介词填空","name":"Unit 8 Idioms 介词填空","instruction":"Fill in the blanks with prepositions or adverbs to make up idioms, phrasal verbs and fixed expressions.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"This truce could last only a short time ___ best and, at worst, would fall apart in a week.","answer":"at","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"It is the custom of Harvard University to confer an honorary degree only ___ someone who is present at the Commencement.","answer":"on","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"These nations' low-cost, high-quality cotton outputs should be competitive, so the poverty of the cotton farmers is laid ___ the door of the U.S. trade practices such as huge subsidies to U.S. cotton growers.","answer":"at","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"He is hostile, disgusted and scornful ___ people full of hatred to him, but respects noble men and knowledgeable scholars.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"\"It had never crossed my mind that the problems could have been related to the surgery I'd had the year before,\" says LeClair. The CT scan images showed several sponges left ___ his intestines.","answer":"behind","type":"text"},{"index":"6","q":"Alipay is ___ alliance with U.S. online payments firm Stripe to make it easier for people in China to buy things from elsewhere in the world.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"7","q":"New media and digital technologies have deprived us ___ the boundary between private life and public activity.","answer":"of","type":"text"},{"index":"8","q":"He is so engaged in the talk because he takes pleasure ___ the rich, delightful lifting of the self through words that find an echo, an amplification, and an emendation in the words of others.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"9","q":"This device is necessary for a long journey because it boasts to inflate your tyres ___ a trice, letting you get back on the road as quickly as possible.","answer":"in","type":"text"},{"index":"10","q":"Dying does not mean one is automatically thrown ___ oblivion.","answer":"into","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-complete-8","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"选词填空","name":"Unit 8 Complete the sentences 选词填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Complete the following sentences with the words and phrases given in the box.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["adept at","be entrapped in","descend into","lay at the door of","inflict","pad out","relish","sanctify","get the credit for","relapse into","oblivion","commensurate","cram","bewitch","leave no room for","laid at the door of","padded out","sanctified","crammed"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"He warned the divided euro zone leaders on Friday that they risked a(n) ___ recession if they failed to press ahead with structural economic reforms.","answer":"relapse into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"For over ten years, the company has been putting its trust in dynamic production inspection solutions and static bench scales in order to ___ error in its inspection process.","answer":"leave no room for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"If the company fails to win back the trust of the consumers, let the blame be first ___ its PR department.","answer":"laid at the door of","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"Many stories and TV dramas are based on the hunt metaphor, the game of a \"bad guy\" being hunted by the \"good guy\", where a cat allows itself to ___ hunting a mouse-like object pulled across a carpet.","answer":"be entrapped in","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"The report was ___ with a lengthy account of the background and extracts from previous documents.","answer":"padded out","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"She accepted the offer to use their beach house with obvious ___.","answer":"relish","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"In the past few decades, the middle class had to maintain its image and its functions, i.e., to consume, so they needed access to credit and had to ___ a class of debt.","answer":"descend into","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"Yelling at or punishing a willfully disobedient child may sometimes be necessary to help the child develop proper character, but it is difficult sometimes for parents to ___ such punishment.","answer":"inflict","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"The group of tribal leaders/rulers are individuals occupying communal political leadership positions by cultural mores and ___ values, and enjoying the legitimacy of particular communities to direct their affairs.","answer":"sanctified","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"Although the recession isn't officially over yet, there is a growing sense that the economy is now in a recovery. But there is also a growing debate about who should ___ the recovery.","answer":"get the credit for","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"11","q":"He was charged for having actually helped create and even exacerbate the crisis, but the credit crunch has saved him from political ___.","answer":"oblivion","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"12","q":"We can offer you a salary that will be ___ with the duties and responsibilities that the job demands.","answer":"commensurate","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"13","q":"This encyclopedia is ___ with information about everything under the sun.","answer":"crammed","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"14","q":"The West End's summer season has the best summer theatre shows to ___ the kids.","answer":"bewitch","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"15","q":"The current technology for creating computerized avatars for human interactions is relatively primitive; future avatars will be ___ manipulating human response such as expressions and body language.","answer":"adept at","type":"text","module":"Box"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cn-en-8","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"汉译英","name":"Unit 8 汉译英","instruction":"Translate the following sentences into English, using the words and phrases from the texts.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"全国正在为重建职业道德规范作出努力。职业道德因素还对事业机构和社会公共部门机构有重要影响，它们传统的优先事项——服务质量和成本管理——需要越来越多地考虑这些影响商业和企业的伦理问题。(restore, take account of)","answer":"A national effort is underway to restore ethical behavior standards. Ethical factors are also a significant influence on social institutions and public sector organizations, for whom the traditional priorities of service quality and cost management must now increasingly take account of these ethical considerations affecting the commercial and corporate world.","type":"text"},{"index":"2","q":"宣布进行独立的国家调查给虐待事件的受害者带来了新的希望，他们一直在哀叹从去年开始事件就缺乏进展。专门小组保证在调查中将\"充分发挥法律的力量\"，在此过程中他们有权强制目击者提供证词。(lament, compel)","answer":"The announcement of an independent national inquiry gives new hope to the victims of abuse who have lamented the lack of progress since last year. The panel pledged to pursue the \"full force of the law\" in the inquiry which has the power to compel witnesses to give evidence.","type":"text"},{"index":"3","q":"文化盲体现为对其他文化的刻板印象或相互轻视。更严重的问题是双方在共同基础上交流和争论的机会被剥夺了。(contempt, deprive)","answer":"Cultural illiteracy is reflected in stereotypes about other cultures or the contempt each side shows for the other. A worse problem is that both sides are deprived of the opportunity to communicate and debate on a common ground.","type":"text"},{"index":"4","q":"漂亮的女人认为没必要拥有聪明才智，也无需知书达理，因为她们在寻找最佳配偶并钓得金龟婿的时候，总能比缺少魅力的竞争者更胜一筹。只有在遇到关乎提升魅力并抬高身价的刺激时，她们的神经元才会\"搭上\"，或是瞬间作出反应。(outstrip, in a trice)","answer":"The beautiful woman sees no need for intelligence nor for understanding because she has always been able to outstrip her less attractive competitors in making the best match and securing the rich husbands. Only in cases of stimuli pertaining to things that will enhance her charms and increase her selling price will her neurones \"connect\", or react to them in a trice.","type":"text"},{"index":"5","q":"支持脱欧的首相竞选人鲍里斯·约翰逊(Boris Johnson)周四的讲话以详尽的竞选宣言模式开始，长篇累牍一一列举\"国家下一任首相\"的计划。然后他声明在咨询了同事并考虑了国会的情况后，他决定退出英国首相的竞选。(pad out, in view of)","answer":"The \"Brexit\" campaigner Boris Johnson began on Thursday in full candidacy announcement mode, and padded out his speech with a list of what he called \"the agenda for the next prime minister of the country\". Then he announced that having consulted colleagues and in view of the circumstances in Parliament, he decided to withdraw from race to become Britain's prime minister.","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-en-cn-8","kind":"translation","kindLabel":"英译汉","name":"Unit 8 英译汉（文学的定义）","instruction":"Translate the following passage into Chinese.","questions":[{"index":"1","q":"What is it that we mean by literature? Popularly, and amongst the thoughtless, it is held to include everything that is printed in a book. Little logic is required to disturb that definition. The most thoughtless person is easily made aware that in the idea of literature one essential element is some relation to a general and common interest of man — so that what applies only to a local, or professional, or merely personal interest, even though presenting itself in the shape of a book, will not belong to Literature.","answer":"我们所说的\"文学\"是什么呢？通俗地说，在不动脑筋的人看来，文学包括印在书里的一切。这个定义不费什么逻辑就能推翻。即使最不动脑筋的人也不难明白：文学的概念中有一个基本要素，就是它与人类的普遍的共同利益有着某种联系——因此，那些只适用于某个地方、某个行业或纯粹个人兴趣的东西，即使印成了书，也不属于文学。","type":"text"}]},{"key":"shangying-3-cloze-8","kind":"wordFill","kindLabel":"完形填空","name":"Unit 8 Cloze 完形填空","modules":["Box"],"instruction":"Read the following passage and fill in the blanks with appropriate words or expressions given in the box. Some words or expressions will not be used.","wordBanks":[{"module":"Box","words":["criteria","examples","include","whose","definitions","view","consists","genre","through","meet"]}],"questions":[{"index":"1","q":"Most (1) ___ of literature have been criterial definitions, definitions based on a list of (2) criteria which all literary works must meet.","answer":"definitions","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"2","q":"(1) Most definitions of literature have been criterial definitions, definitions based on a list of (2) ___ which all literary works must meet.","answer":"criteria","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"3","q":"Some critics believe that literature is a canon which (3) ___ of those works in language by which a community defines itself (4) the course of its history.","answer":"consists","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"4","q":"(3) Some critics believe that literature is a canon which consists of those works in language by which a community defines itself (4) ___ the course of its history.","answer":"through","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"5","q":"It includes works primarily artistic and also those (5) ___ aesthetic qualities are only secondary.","answer":"whose","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"6","q":"However, more current theories of meaning take the (6) ___ that definitions are based on prototypes:","answer":"view","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"7","q":"there is broad agreement about good examples that (7) ___ all of the prototypical characteristics,","answer":"meet","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"8","q":"and other (8) ___ are related to the prototypes by family resemblance.","answer":"examples","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"9","q":"For literary works, prototypical characteristics (9) ___ careful use of language,","answer":"include","type":"text","module":"Box"},{"index":"10","q":"being written in a literary (10) ___ (poetry, prose fiction, or drama), being read aesthetically, and containing many weak implicatures.","answer":"genre","type":"text","module":"Box"}]}]},{"key":"shangying-4","name":"商英教程4","units":[]}]};